{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K5Lu91eoVnKwJVroHDUqzx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Revamp — Implementation Plan (Crucible Stage 2)\n2\t\n3\t**Forged via Crucible** (researchPrime → Crucible → Foreman trio) · 2026-06-06\n4\t**Status:** Stage 0 (North Star locked) ✅ · Stage 1 (Master Plan, converged) ✅ · Stage 2 (this doc) — wave decomposition for Foreman handoff.\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## North Star (locked 2026-06-06)\n9\t\n10\t> Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value** *and* run on a **robust Foreman/Crucible-style\n11\t> agentic architecture** — as **co-equal goals**. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the\n12\t> library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and\n13\t> curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine.\n14\t\n15\t**Locked-preserved assets (off-limits to break):** KB SQLite schema + browsable library · security\n16\tgating (quarantine + injection sanitizer + license gate) · deterministic cost telemetry · Helping\n17\tHand (aurora-kb MCP) + publisher to the private repo.\n18\t\n19\t**Substrate decision:** metered **API is the default** (the cost bug is already fixed via\n20\t`thinking_budget=0`). Flat-rate **Claude Max + Gemini Ultra** are an **optional, spike-gated\n21\ttransport**, never the foundation — a prior adversarial round proved a flat-rate-only foundation\n22\twould silently zero-out the cost telemetry (a locked asset) and is fragile for unattended use.\n23\tEmbeddings stay on API.\n24\t\n25\t**Architecture vehicle:** the Foreman/Crucible **pattern** (fresh-context sub-agents +\n26\tadversarial EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX iteration), **not** Foreman's wave-to-done **engine** (a category\n27\terror for open-ended discovery). When durability primitives are eventually needed, **reimplement\n28\t~100 LOC in Python — do not link Foreman** (Aurora is Python; the SQLite DB is already the real\n29\tcheckpoint).\n30\t\n31\t---\n32\t\n33\t## How we got here (the reframe)\n34\t\n35\tThe original ask was \"rebuild Aurora as a Foreman-style swarm.\" Crucible's adversarial review\n36\t(3 Sharks + 2 code-grounded investigators + an independent Judge) found that **~70% of the felt\n37\tpain is an unwired \"consume\" loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine.** Aurora's *produce*\n38\thalf works (889 artifacts, nightly briefings generated); the *consume* half was dead at every\n39\tbridge. The architecture worth building now is the **thin judgment slice** (a confidence badge),\n40\tnot the parallel fan-out — which is \"engineering theater\" at the current `TOP_K=2`.\n41\t\n42\t**Three distinct \"fan-outs\" — only the third was cut:**\n43\t1. **Discovery swarm (scouts)** — parallel material-gathering. Exists (`scout.fan_out`). *Kept; upgraded in Wave 5.*\n44\t2. **Serial judgment loop** — validates the K best finds one-at-a-time. Exists. K=2.\n45\t3. **Judgment fan-out** — parallelizing #2. *Deferred behind a tripwire (below).*\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## Wave decomposition (thin-vertical-first)\n50\t\n51\tOrdered so the first architecture we build is the part John can *feel*. ~7–11 dev-days for\n52\tWaves 0–5; the deferred layer is cut until its tripwire fires.\n53\t\n54\t### Wave 0 — Re-light Helping Hand  ✅ DONE (2026-06-06)\n55\t**Done-when:** the recommender fires in a Cowork session again.\n56\t- [x] Project `.mcp.json` threshold `0.42 → 0.25`.\n57\t- [x] Home-dir `~/.claude/.mcp.json` threshold `0.65 → 0.25` (second drift the fix exposed).\n58\t- [x] Drift-checker (`bin/check-hh-threshold-drift.py`) extended to watch the **project-scoped**\n59\t      `.mcp.json` — closes the blind spot that let the regression recur silently. Now 6/6 sources\n60\t      agree at 0.25 (exit 0).\n61\t- [x] **John action:** enable the `aurora-kb` MCP server in Cowork for `C:\\dev\\aurora`\n62\t      (`mcpServers:[]` → approved). Verified 2026-06-06: `recent_summary` responded live\n63\t      in-session (KB returns counts), so the server is enabled and reachable.\n64\t\n65\t### Wave 1 — Make the output visible\n66\t**Done-when:** John sees the briefing without opening a folder, and the library index is navigable.\n67\t- Push the morning briefing to where John lives (toast / email / auto-surfaced session note) —\n68\t  today it is only written to disk + pushed to a private repo.\n69\t- Fix the `library/index.md` join: it renders `(unplaced) ? (?)` for all 889 rows because the\n70\t  `embeddings.domain_path` / `complexity_rank` join is broken. Restore the domain × complexity view.\n71\t- **Acceptance:** Given a completed nightly sweep, When the briefing job runs, Then John receives a\n72\t  notification with the top finds; And `library/index.md` shows real domains/complexity for ≥95% of\n73\t  placed artifacts.\n74\t\n75\t### Wave 2 — Security-gate single-owner + backfill (architecture keystone)\n76\t**Done-when:** the gate predicate has exactly one definition and `security_status` is populated.\n77\t- De-duplicate `gate_predicate_sql()` — the literal `security_status IN ('clean','clean-with-notes')`\n78\t  is currently inlined in 3 places (`server.py:333`, `publisher.py:61`, `publisher.py:218-219`)\n79\t  besides the owner (`roles/security/gate.py`). Make all enforcement points import the helper.\n80\t- Add a CI grep test that fails if the literal appears anywhere except `gate.py`.\n81\t- Backfill `security_status` (NULL on all 889 rows today — a latent landmine: flipping enforce mode\n82\t  would empty the KB from every query).\n83\t- **Acceptance:** Given the repo, When the CI test runs, Then the servable literal exists in exactly\n84\t  one file; And no artifact has NULL `security_status`; And enforce-mode no longer empties queries.\n85\t\n86\t### Wave 3 — Evidence-rigor fix-loop → confidence badge (the keystone)\n87\t**Done-when:** each curation carries a `verified | documented | lossy` confidence badge, produced by\n88\tan adversarial loop that iterates *evidence*, never the verdict.\n89\t- Add an EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX→RE-REVIEW loop to the judgment slice (runner + critics + reconciler).\n90\t  The \"fix\" step is a **deterministic evidence-deepener** (expand the corpus by the next N chars /\n91\t  referenced files **in declared order** — never LLM-chosen excerpts) triggered by critic\n92\t  disagreement or abstain. Critics then re-score the *enriched* bundle.\n93\t- **Conservative-bias is structural:** the loop can only *add evidence*; the gate is monotonic\n94\t  toward reject. Exit on (a) disagreement ≤ 0.4 → reduce as-is; (b) `MAX_EVIDENCE_ITERS` (2) without\n95\t  convergence → force-downgrade to `flag`; (c) any `injection_risk ≥ 0.7` or `reject` vote → reject\n96\t  immediately. No agent in the loop can write the verdict (the security verdict is written only by\n97\t  the reduce step). This is the answer to \"a fix-loop optimizes toward pass\" — it structurally can't.\n98\t- Emit the badge from the prov-edge vocabulary already in the codebase: converged-at-iter-0 with 3\n99\t  agreeing critics = `verified`; needed deepening = `documented`; force-downgraded = `lossy`.\n100\t- **Value-loop hook:** surface the badge + the reconciler's one-paragraph incorporation note in the\n101\t  briefing's \"notable this week\" block and let Helping Hand rank/filter on it.\n102\t- **Acceptance:** Given a candidate, When validated, Then it has a badge + incorporation note;\n103\t  And no path produces `pass` that the evidence didn't earn; And the briefing/HH show the badge.\n104\t\n105\t### Wave 4 — Trustworthy cost numbers\n106\t**Done-when:** the cost ledger reflects real spend.\n107\t- Replace the \"UNVERIFIED guesses\" in `kb/pricing.yaml` with real Google/Anthropic SKU rates.\n108\t- Meter the MCP server's query-embedding path (`server.py:_embed_query`) — currently unmetered.\n109\t- Verify the `thinking_budget=0` fix on a live run; keep the `thoughts_token_count` fold + unpriced-\n110\t  model warn-once (both load-bearing per the May incident).\n111\t- **Acceptance:** Given a nightly run, When costs roll up, Then every LLM call is metered against a\n112\t  pricing.yaml key that matches the model tag used at call time (the exact May bug, regression-tested).\n113\t\n114\t### Wave 5 — Scout memory / source-reputation  *(added from John's insight)*\n115\t**Done-when:** the discovery swarm prioritizes sources that have historically yielded quality, while\n116\tstill exploring new ones — and source quality is visible.\n117\t- Track per-source yield: which sources produced `verified`/accepted artifacts vs noise.\n118\t- Explore/exploit seed prioritization: weight revisits toward high-yield sources, reserve a budget\n119\t  for new exploration. (Respect the existing 2-curator + 3-night-shadow promotion rule.)\n120\t- Surface a source-quality signal per artifact in the library + briefing (pain #6).\n121\t- **Note:** this is also the natural down-payment on the deferred learning loop.\n122\t- **Acceptance:** Given N nights of history, When a sweep plans its scout pass, Then high-yield\n123\t  sources are prioritized and a measurable exploration budget is spent on new sources; And each\n124\t  artifact shows a source-quality indicator.\n125\t\n126\t---\n127\t\n128\t## Deferred behind a tripwire — judgment fan-out (#3)\n129\t\n130\t**Cut for now.** Build the asyncio judgment fan-out + single WAL write-actor + durable checkpoints\n131\t**only when both hold:** `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K ≥ ~20` (a 10× increase from 2) **AND** a measured\n132\tserial-latency pain. Until then the serial loop is fine and the SQLite DB is the real checkpoint.\n133\tWhen triggered: reimplement ~100 LOC of checkpoint/budget primitives in Python (don't link Foreman);\n134\trun the security judge in the read-only worker and confine row-writes to the single write-actor;\n135\tderive resume state from the DB (existence of a `validations` row), not a side checkpoint file.\n136\t\n137\t**Likely trigger:** if John decides Aurora should validate many more finds per night (raise K), that\n138\tsame decision flips this from theater to worthwhile. Revisit as a conditional second Crucible study.\n139\t\n140\t---\n141\t\n142\t## Migration / shadow / rollback (applies to Waves 2–3)\n143\t\n144\t- `AURORA_ENGINE=legacy|fanout` env flag; default `legacy`. Both write the same schema.\n145\t- `--shadow` mode runs both engines over the identical candidate list; the new engine writes to a\n146\t  mirror `validations_shadow` table and **cannot** write a servable verdict during shadow.\n147\t- `bin/engine-diff.py` joins legacy vs shadow per slug. **Promotion gate:** verdict-match ≥ 95% on\n148\t  ≥200 candidates, **zero** cases where new says `pass` and legacy said `flag/reject`, cost ≤ 1.5× legacy.\n149\t- Keep legacy code for a 1-week rollback window (repo convention). Rollback = one env var.\n150\t\n151\t---\n152\t\n153\t## Foreman handoff (next gate)\n154\t\n155\tStage 2 hands off to Foreman only after this plan passes Foreman's well-formedness gate\n156\t(`node foreman/bin/locate-plan.mjs --json <dir>`, exit 0). Each wave above has a one-line *done-when*\n157\t+ Given/When/Then acceptance criteria so Foreman can drive EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX→RE-REVIEW per wave.\n158\t\n159\t## Effort summary\n160\t\n161\t| Wave | Effort | Goal served |\n162\t|---|---|---|\n163\t| 0 Re-light HH | done (mins) | Value |\n164\t| 1 Visible output | ~1 day | Value |\n165\t| 2 Gate single-owner + backfill | ~1.5 days | Both (keystone) |\n166\t| 3 Evidence fix-loop + badge | ~3–4 days | **Both** |\n167\t| 4 Trustworthy cost | ~1–2 days | Value (trust) |\n168\t| 5 Scout memory / source-rep | ~2–3 days | Both (+ learning down-payment) |\n169\t| ~~Judgment fan-out~~ | deferred | — |\n170\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp7xYPhNGPdp6bdeA6FWy","session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"308a3152-c188-47c3-b8f1-4cc2fe72dbe2","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:12:17.089Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace Aurora strategic trajectory"}
