{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMJANjyvhDvn8yQ9wfJgg2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing — Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1, rev 3 — post Shark rounds 1+2)\n2\t\n3\t**Forged via Crucible** · 2026-06-09 · Stage 0 locked ✅ · Stage 1 rev 3 (two adversarial rounds incorporated; Judge + user gate pending)\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-09)\n8\t\n9\t> **Objective:** Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting,\n10\t> and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed, measurable value loop —\n11\t> built by evolving the existing pipeline, never touching the proven plumbing.\n12\t\n13\t**Criteria (every plan element must serve ≥1 — the inclusion test):**\n14\t1. **Right kind at ingest** — arxiv can never land as `tool`/`agent` again; vendor blog posts and\n15\t   awesome-list pointers never become first-class tools; OpenRouter is a reference table, never \"finds.\"\n16\t2. **Top finds respect attention** — named, ranked, real artifacts with a one-line \"why this matters\n17\t   to John\" and a quality signal; never raw IDs.\n18\t3. **A persisted taste score** — interestingness tuned to John's profile, computed at ingest, stored,\n19\t   driving all ranking.\n20\t4. **The value loop closes on real data** — productivity_index derives from actual `hh_events` usage;\n21\t   \"did this help\" is captured and feeds back into ranking.\n22\t5. **The catalog is trustworthy** — existing noise backfilled, dupes merged, stale entries retire on\n23\t   policy, reported counts honest.\n24\t6. **Felt immediately, weekly thereafter** — Wave 1 changes tomorrow morning's briefing; the weekly\n25\t   digest ships in an early wave (it is papers' only push surface).\n26\t\n27\t**Stage-0 gate decisions (John, 2026-06-09):** papers = opt-in stream (`kind='paper'`, never in top\n28\tfinds/finds counts/push surfaces; \"papers worth reading\" in the weekly digest) · vendor blog posts\n29\trejected at ingest (existing 50 nvidia rows retired in backfill) · taste scorer approved at\n30\tcents/night (metered, capped).\n31\t\n32\t**Stage-1 gate decisions (DECIDED by John, 2026-06-09):**\n33\t- **D1 — Helping Hand match pool, models: mode-scoped exclusion.** `kind='model'` excluded from\n34\t  single-mode routing/auto-load and from surfaced-event telemetry; models stay recallable in\n35\t  explicit ranked/compare queries (the documented compare path, `server.py:707-773`, keeps working).\n36\t  Context: 27 of 98 surfaced events were models, 0 ever loaded.\n37\t- **D2 — Helping Hand match pool, papers: matchable in pull, labeled.** Papers never pushed (no top\n38\t  finds, no counts, no auto-load) but direct pull queries can find them, clearly kind-labeled —\n39\t  migration 0012's original intent preserved.\n40\t\n41\t**Hard constraints (locked):** preserve KB SQLite schema (additive migrations only) + browsable\n42\tlibrary + security gating (single-owner gate) + deterministic cost telemetry + Helping Hand MCP +\n43\tpublisher. Metered API default. 915 tests stay green; no weakening; count may only rise. OUT:\n44\tdiscovery parallelism; issue #5 (H1 fetch reliability).\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## Evidence base (E1–E12 session-reproduced; E13–E23 added/corrected by Shark rounds 1–2)\n49\t\n50\t| # | Finding | Evidence |\n51\t|---|---|---|\n52\t| E1 | 40% of `tool` rows are noise: 58 arxiv + 50 developer.nvidia.com + 31 awesome-list pointers of 346 | DB 2026-06-09 |\n53\t| E2 | 45% of `agent` rows (38/84) arxiv; 10 newest agents ALL arxiv | DB |\n54\t| E3 | `kind='paper'` exists (CHECK + 109 rows) but only via the manual `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`; ingest stamps kind by sweep (`static_screener.py:34`); `upsert_artifact` never updates kind on existing rows (`librarian.py:250-254`) → backfill is load-bearing for existing rows | code |\n55\t| E4 | `top_finds` = 5 newest today by `id DESC`, only models excluded — no ranking (`morning_briefing.py:1075-1083`) | code |\n56\t| E5 | No interestingness score anywhere; reconciler `incorporation_note` covers only 16 artifacts ever (TOP_K=2/sweep), none recent | code+DB |\n57\t| E6 | `productivity_index` reads starved `hh_interaction_buffer`; real signal in `hh_events`: 98 surfaced / 6 loaded / 1 dismissed across **20 distinct queries, 5 with ≥1 load**; each query surfaces up to 10 candidates → per-event ratios are structurally capped (~10–30%); per-query adoption is the meaningful shape | code+DB |\n58\t| E7 | `log_use` already promotes hh_events outcomes (capture built; read side isn't); no usage→ranking feedback | code |\n59\t| E8 | `link_health` 0 rows but `bin/check_link_health.py` is complete + tested (gh stars, stale_url, rename; 7-day idempotency; **append-per-probe rows → N-consecutive-stale queries are implementable**); it was simply never scheduled; publisher already gates on `stale_url` | code |\n60\t| E9 | `confidence_badge` NULL on ~all recent rows; `source_quality` = 'high' on effectively every recent find incl. today's nvidia post (it is seed-yield reputation, not artifact quality) → any rank keyed on them degenerates to recency | DB |\n61\t| E10 | No weekly digest; daily briefing only | code |\n62\t| E11 | Models excluded from `top_finds`/briefing counts but counted by `recent_summary` (no retired/kind filter, `server.py:1386-1391`) and present in the match pool (340/350 with vectors) | code+DB |\n63\t| E12 | Real value exists: 48 clean skills, 207 GitHub tools, notable frameworks | DB |\n64\t| E13 | Real schedule: Agents 01:07, Skills 02:19, Tools 03:41, Models 05:03, Briefing 06:47; publisher chained inside sweep + briefing `.cmd`s (runs ~01:30 too). **Scheduled tasks execute `C:\\dev\\aurora` directly — the dirty working tree IS production** | Get-ScheduledTask + setup-tasks.ps1:76-82 |\n65\t| E14 | HH `match_request` has no kind filter (`server.py:508-516, 567-575`); HH runtime is the **installed plugin** — server.py changes require `bin/build-plugin.py` rebuild + reinstall | code |\n66\t| E15 | Library is a filesystem surface: 109 dead `papers/<slug>/` links exist TODAY (grid links by DB kind; `library/papers/` absent); superseded pages never scrubbed outside security-enforce; **publisher copytree ships whatever is on disk** | code+fs |\n67\t| E16 | `migrate_to_kind_paper.py` re-run would DELETE 3 legitimate Agentic-Home skills (ids 822-824 match its fixture heuristic) — its delete step must never run again | code+DB |\n68\t| E17 | No priced flash-lite key in pricing.yaml; unpriced tags meter $0 warn-once (`llm.py:146-147`); `default_models` is test-validated but **runtime-inert** — live role selection is env-based (`AURORA_*_MODEL`) | code |\n69\t| E18 | Test blast radius small: top_finds/session_note shape only in `test_wave1_visibility.py`; live-DB tests tolerant; publisher harness exists (`test_snapshot_scrub.py`, `security/test_integration_e2e.py:285-337`) | tests |\n70\t| E19 | **Simulated draft ranking on real data:** day 06-07 would headline John's own locally-ingested `crucible`/`foreman`/`researchPrime` (`local:` URLs, kind=skill); 06-08 would include an openai.com blog post and a saturnci.com `.html` page (both source_quality 'high'). Denylist-only filtering fails; a positive eligibility gate is required | DB simulation |\n71\t| E20 | `_artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot` early-returns True when `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE != 'enforce'` (`publisher.py:78-79`) and production runs mode-unset → a retired check inside the gate body would be **dead code in production** | code+.env |\n72\t| E21 | Scout-level awesome-list fix already exists (links → `discovery_queue`, `scout.py:216-254`); the live leak is the **drain path** (a drained repo that is itself a link list becomes a first-class artifact, e.g. id 907 + pointer rows 886-906, newest 2026-06-05); `screen()` has no DB handle → fix needs the `_DISCOVERED_LINKS` buffer + orchestrator-flush pattern | code+DB |\n73\t| E22 | `write_library_md` consumes sweep-time dataclasses (Candidate/ScreenedCandidate/EmbeddingPlacement), has no paper template; **dir-MOVE of existing pages + `regenerate_indexes` (DB-kind-driven links) is the lossless path** and preserves AURORA-CURATED cards (skip-guard at `librarian.py:643-651`) | code |\n74\t| E23 | `run-morning-briefing.cmd` has no error gating (a failing inserted line cannot block the briefing) but line 6 truncates the shared log with `>` — an inserted backfill must log elsewhere | code |\n75\t\n76\t## Assumption map\n77\t- **Confirmed:** E1–E23 (all code/DB-grounded; E13/E19/E20/E21 corrected or established by Sharks).\n78\t- **Inferred (verify in Stage 2):** arxiv v1/v2 dupe set size; gh token rate budget for the stars backfill.\n79\t- **Gaps:** none blocking; Stage-2 list below.\n80\t\n81\t## Premortem (top risks → mitigations)\n82\t\n83\t| Risk | Mitigation |\n84\t|---|---|\n85\t| Dirty working tree is production (E13) | Deploy gate every wave: clean committed tree before the 01:07 window; W1 = one reviewed commit before 06:47 |\n86\t| Backfill deletes/retires wrong rows (E16) | Re-kind/retire only, never DELETE; `--dry-run` + `--audit-out` mandatory; migrate script's delete step is dead |\n87\t| Re-kind/retire orphans library pages; publisher ships them (E15, E20) | Backfills own the filesystem via **dir-move** + `regenerate_indexes`, delete superseded dirs idempotently on every run; publisher `retired_at` predicate evaluated **before** the security-mode early-return, tested with mode unset |\n88\t| Top finds headline self-finds/blogspam (E19) | **Positive eligibility gate**: GitHub-hosted (github_full_name or github.com URL) OR confidence_badge present; exclude `local:`/self-curated; vendor denylist as belt-and-braces |\n89\t| productivity_index prints a meaningless 0%/6% (E6) | Defined formula: **per-query suggestion adoption** (see W1); window widens until ≥10 queries else all-time, labeled; sample size always shown |\n90\t| Taste scorer meters $0 (E17) | Priced key + `default_models.taste` + `AURORA_TASTE_MODEL` env resolve to provably the same tag; tests assert non-zero usd_estimate |\n91\t| HH changes silently don't ship (E14) | Any server.py wave ends with plugin rebuild + reinstall + live smoke |\n92\t| Feedback loop self-reinforces | Usage modifier bounded + decaying, on top of interest_score; profile is John-edited only (drift hints, no auto-mutation) |\n93\t| §4 verbatim contract breaks | Additive JSON fields only; `test_wave1_visibility.py` updated additively |\n94\t| Overnight window W1→W2: tonight's sweeps still ingest mis-kinded rows; ~01:30 publisher ships them until the backfill lands in W2 | Accepted, time-boxed: W1's briefing-side exclusions hide them from John; W2 (immediately next) adds ingest routing + backfill + .cmd hooks |\n95\t\n96\t---\n97\t\n98\t## Wave plan (5 waves, thin-vertical-first; sizes honest per Shark round 2)\n99\t\n100\t### Wave 1 (S) — Tomorrow's briefing (felt vertical; two briefing-only files + tests, one commit before 06:47)\n101\t**Serves 2, 4(partial), 5(partial), 6.** Touches `morning_briefing.py` + `briefing_delivery.py`\n102\t(session_note top-find lines + productivity line are rendered there, `briefing_delivery.py:80-97` —\n103\tJudge condition) + additive tests ONLY. Neither file is executed by the 01:07 sweeps\n104\t(briefing_delivery is imported only by morning_briefing), so the deadline is 06:47.\n105\t- **top_finds v2:** positive eligibility gate (GitHub-hosted OR badge present; exclude `local:`),\n106\t  kind-agnostic noise exclusions in the query (arxiv URL/slug patterns from\n107\t  `migrate_to_kind_paper.py:115-125`, vendor denylist, pointer-description match, `kind NOT IN\n108\t  ('model','paper')`); rank = badge → kind-priority (skill>agent>tool>template) → recency; emit\n109\t  additive fields `name/kind/why/quality`; `why` = sanitized one-sentence short_description\n110\t  (U+FFFD stripped; explicitly interim until W4's `interest_why`); `quality` rendered **only when\n111\t  discriminating** (badge or stars present), omitted otherwise. session_note renders the same lines.\n112\t- **productivity_index v2 (defined formula):** suggestion adoption = (queries with ≥1 `loaded`) /\n113\t  (distinct queries surfaced) from `hh_events`, window auto-widens 7d→all-time until ≥10 queries\n114\t  (fallback labeled); JSON carries `window`, `sample_size`, and the metric surfaced as\n115\t  **\"suggestion adoption\"**; `no_data` only when zero queries ever.\n116\t- **Honest counts:** `finds_new` excludes papers via the same kind-agnostic URL/slug exclusions\n117\t  (works even though tonight's rows are still mis-kinded).\n118\t- **Done-when:** next session_note: zero raw IDs, every top find a named eligible artifact with a\n119\t  why-line; adoption metric + sample size shown; committed clean before 06:47; suite green\n120\t  (additive updates to `test_wave1_visibility.py` only).\n121\t\n122\t### Wave 2 (L) — Right kind at ingest + catalog backfills + serving-surface trust\n123\t**Serves 1, 5.**\n124\t- **Ingest routing (`static_screener.py`):** arxiv → `kind='paper'` at screen time; source-type gate\n125\t  (vendor/blog denylist + non-repo heuristic; rejects audited).\n126\t- **Drain-path pointer fix (E21):** a drained repo that is itself a link list re-enqueues its links\n127\t  into the existing `discovery_queue` (`_DISCOVERED_LINKS` buffer + orchestrator flush) instead of\n128\t  becoming a candidate; screen-time pointer-description reject as backstop. (Orchestrator wiring\n129\t  budgeted — this is multi-file by necessity.)\n130\t- **`bin/backfill_paper_kind.py`:** re-kind the ~96 arxiv tool/agent rows (UPDATE only, no deletes);\n131\t  filesystem owned by **dir-move** `library/{agents,tools}/<slug>/ → library/papers/<slug>/`\n132\t  (page-write fallback only where no source dir; preserves curated cards) + `regenerate_indexes`\n133\t  (heals the 109 pre-existing dead links); deletes superseded dirs **idempotently on every run**;\n134\t  `--dry-run` + `--audit-out`; own log file (E23); hooked into `run-morning-briefing.cmd` AND\n135\t  `run-agents.cmd` ahead of their publisher calls.\n136\t- **Retire backfills** (retire = `retired_at`, never DELETE; dry-run + audit each): 50 nvidia rows,\n137\t  the ~31-34 pointer rows (exact set reconciled in the `--dry-run --audit-out` pass — Judge nit),\n138\t  arxiv v1/v2 dupes (keep latest, alias old); library pages of retired rows removed, indexes\n139\t  regenerated.\n140\t- **Publisher:** unconditional `retired_at` predicate evaluated **before** the security-mode\n141\t  early-return (E20); snapshot scrubs retired pages; regression tests run with\n142\t  `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` unset (extend `test_snapshot_scrub.py`).\n143\t- **Helping Hand server (per D1/D2):** `recent_summary` filters retired + stops counting\n144\t  models/papers as finds; match pool scoped per gate decisions; **plugin rebuild + reinstall +\n145\t  live smoke** in done-when.\n146\t- **`bin/noise_audit.py`:** standing zero-noise check (arxiv-as-tool/agent, vendor tools, pointer\n147\t  artifacts, dead library links, retired-leaks-in-surfaces) + fixture tests; failure surfaces in the\n148\t  nightly summary. Cross-surface count regression tests land HERE (counts must be consistent from\n149\t  this wave on).\n150\t- **Done-when:** noise audit returns 0 on the live KB; retired rows absent from snapshot,\n151\t  recent_summary, and library; mis-kind regression impossible (fixture tests on screener + drain\n152\t  path); suite green.\n153\t\n154\t### Wave 3 (S-M) — Weekly digest v1 + notability signal\n155\t**Serves 2, 5, 6.**\n156\t- **Schedule the existing probe:** register `bin/check_link_health.py` weekly in `setup-tasks.ps1`\n157\t  + one supervised backfill run (gh-CLI token; 7-day idempotency). Done-when: ≥500 of the ~700\n158\t  active GitHub-linked artifacts probed, `gh_stargazers` populated.\n159\t- **`bin/weekly_digest.py` + scheduled task:** \"what's genuinely worth knowing this week\" —\n160\t  heuristic-ranked top finds of the week (W1 eligibility gate + stars now available) with why-lines;\n161\t  **papers worth reading** (the Stage-0 opt-in stream); catalog-health deltas (retired/deduped/new).\n162\t  Delivered via `briefing_delivery` (toast + session_note pointer); `reports/weekly/`.\n163\t- **Done-when:** digest #1 generated from real KB data and delivered; stars visible in top-find\n164\t  quality signals where present; suite green.\n165\t\n166\t### Wave 4 (M) — The taste score\n167\t**Serves 2, 3.**\n168\t- **Pricing first:** priced pricing.yaml key for the chosen taste model (+ `verification:` block);\n169\t  `roles/taste.py` resolves its model from `default_models.taste` with `AURORA_TASTE_MODEL` env\n170\t  override — priced key and called tag provably identical (extends `test_pricing_keys.py`,\n171\t  asserts non-zero usd_estimate).\n172\t- **Migration (additive):** `artifacts.interest_score REAL`, `interest_why TEXT`, `interest_scored_at TEXT`.\n173\t- **`roles/taste.py`:** nightly scorer for new non-paper finds against versioned, John-editable\n174\t  `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`; inputs: short_description + incorporation_note + stars + kind;\n175\t  metered via CostRecorder, nightly call cap, heuristic fallback (stars+badge+kind-priority).\n176\t  **Precedence:** `interest_why` drives ranking surfaces; `incorporation_note` stays the library\n177\t  \"how to incorporate\" voice.\n178\t- **Ranking switch:** top_finds + digest order by `interest_score` (stars/quality as features);\n179\t  why-lines upgrade from descriptions to `interest_why`.\n180\t- **Done-when:** every new find scored with why-line; cost rows non-zero and capped; rankings use\n181\t  the score; suite green.\n182\t\n183\t### Wave 5 (S-M) — Close the loop\n184\t**Serves 4, 5.**\n185\t- **Bounded usage modifier:** loaded boosts / dismissed decays (bounded, decaying) applied in HH\n186\t  match ranking and top-finds/digest ranking on top of interest_score; fixture-tested; plugin\n187\t  rebuild + reinstall + smoke.\n188\t- **Retirement policy** (thin layer over existing machinery): N=2 consecutive stale probes → retire\n189\t  (link_health is append-per-probe, E22-verified implementable); never-surfaced + low interest +\n190\t  old → retire; nightly, audited, reversible. **Acceptance is fixture-based** (live stale-retirements\n191\t  need ~2 weeks of probe history by design — stated, not hidden).\n192\t- **Digest value section:** suggestion-adoption trend, loads/dismissals, **profile-drift hints**\n193\t  (most-dismissed kinds/domains vs profile emphases → prompts a manual profile edit; no auto-mutation).\n194\t- **Done-when:** fixture events demonstrably shift ranking; policy runs nightly unattended (fixture\n195\t  acceptance + live leg armed with N=2); digest shows the value section; suite green.\n196\t\n197\t---\n198\t\n199\t## Cut list (Grasscatcher)\n200\t- Discovery parallelism / judgment fan-out — locked out (theater at TOP_K=2).\n201\t- Issue #5 (H1 fetch reliability) — separately tracked.\n202\t- Semantic/embedding dedupe — canonical-URL + arxiv-version dedupe covers observed dupes.\n203\t- A `reference` kind for vendor posts — rejected at Stage-0 gate.\n204\t- Briefing delivery rework — the pipe works.\n205\t- Multi-user personalization — one user; a profile file suffices.\n206\t- Full back-catalog taste re-scoring — score new finds + backfill survivors reaching a serving surface.\n207\t- Rebuilding the stars probe — `check_link_health.py` exists; we schedule it.\n208\t- Feeding `hh_interaction_buffer` — fails the inclusion test once the index reads `hh_events`.\n209\t- Auto-mutating the interest profile from usage — self-reinforcement risk; drift hints only.\n210\t- Paper page **regeneration** in the backfill — dir-move is lossless and preserves curated cards (E22).\n211\t\n212\t## Stage-2 verification list (code-grounding before freeze)\n213\t1. HH server scorer internals → exact shape of the W5 modifier.\n214\t2. gh token/rate budget for the ~700-artifact stars backfill.\n215\t3. Exact arxiv v1/v2 dupe set for the W2 dedupe.\n216\t4. The non-repo heuristic for the W2 source-type gate (false-positive audit against the 207 real GitHub tools + non-GitHub legit tools).\n217\t5. `_DISCOVERED_LINKS` flush mechanics for the drain-path fix.\n218\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp7xYPhNGPdp6bdeA6FWy","session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"46b1f612-e7a7-40dd-aa2a-5b15bf6bdbb6","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:12:23.897Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace Aurora strategic trajectory"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fgq2TJDbbd3mNXZJcf89TR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Crucible Stage 0 — Intake & Framing: Aurora Awareness Revamp\n2\t\n3\t**Run:** 2026-06-11. **Mode:** brownfield-on-existing-data. **Substrate:** subscription + Node engine.\n4\t**Inputs:** `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md`, `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md` (adversarially validated).\n5\t**This is the LOCK gate.** Nothing is planned until you lock §1. Drift detection begins after the lock.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. NORTH STAR — to be LOCKED verbatim (HANDOFF §1, John's intent)\n10\t\n11\t> Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic\n12\t> systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them,\n13\t> the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools** — serving THREE co-equal jobs:\n14\t> (1) **educate John**, (2) **guide his generation of new agents**, (3) **feed the agentic\n15\t> systems + Claude + Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.**\n16\t>\n17\t> **Drift guard:** every proposed surface or collection change must serve **awareness +\n18\t> adoption-decision + agent-feeding**. A prettier ops console or richer taxonomy that does\n19\t> not make John *more aware and better-decided* is bloat (fails the inclusion test).\n20\t\n21\t### North-Star success criteria (the measurable spine — every wave must serve ≥1)\n22\t- **NS1 — Awareness:** John can see, per category (skills/tools/templates/agents/**models**),\n23\t  \"what is current best-in-class + what newly moved + why it matters\" without leaving his\n24\t  morning report / a glance at one surface.\n25\t- **NS2 — Model+benchmark intelligence:** the 352 already-collected priced models are\n26\t  surfaced, and at least a thin slice of benchmarks is collected and joined — answering\n27\t  \"which model for X, at what price/perf\" as a decision.\n28\t- **NS3 — Adoption decision:** candidate skills/tools/agents reach John as a fast,\n29\t  trustworthy *should-I-adopt?* decision (summary/risks/advantages/why/effort), and accepted\n30\t  ones feed Helping Hand.\n31\t- **NS4 — Right collection:** the nightly spend buys frontier-relevant agentic-AI items\n32\t  (harnesses/models/benchmarks/high-signal skills-tools-templates), **without losing recall\n33\t  on the obscure small-author find.**\n34\t- **NS5 — Honest value:** John gets a plain-English, no-vanity answer to \"is this working and\n35\t  worth its dollar,\" with sample sizes shown and rates suppressed when ground truth is too thin.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## 2. Brownfield ingest — what exists, labeled (Confirmed / Inferred / Gap)\n40\t\n41\t**Reuse, don't rebuild** (AuroraTwo verdict + your constraint):\n42\t- **[Confirmed]** Read-only dashboard package `dashboard/` (blueprint-mountable), `aurora_dashboard.py`, port 5001. Shipped 2026-06-11.\n43\t- **[Confirmed]** `kb/aurora.db`: `artifacts`, `models` (352 rows, all priced), `model_benchmarks` (**0 rows**), `embeddings.domain_path`, `link_health`, `hh_events`, `costs`, `runs`.\n44\t- **[Confirmed]** `reports/` (morning briefing — John: \"fine\"), `helping-hand-plugin/` (KB MCP), `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`, `roles/taste.py` (interest_score on ~30 finds + heuristic fallback).\n45\t- **[Confirmed]** Nightly sweeps real schedule 01:07–06:47; publisher pushes scrubbed snapshot to `aurora-library`.\n46\t- **[Confirmed, from RESEARCH §B]** `hh_events`: 106 events, only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed), 21 queries / 10 sessions / 3 weeks. → metrics ground truth is near-zero; learned signals run open-loop.\n47\t- **[Confirmed]** `models` has junk rows (`-1000000` price sentinel; `$0` rows).\n48\t- **[Inferred]** Per-sweep deltas (\"what was new\") already computed/stored (dashboard W4) → promotable to a momentum view cheaply.\n49\t- **[Gap]** No benchmark collection. No model surface. No actionable adoption queue. No human-readable value/health. No relationship map John wants. Collection skewed to arxiv (8 papers / 0 skills-tools-agents last night).\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## 3. Scope (the §4 deltas, as framed for planning) — IN, OUT, CONSTRAINED\n54\t\n55\t**IN scope (serves NS1–NS5):**\n56\t1. **Model-intelligence surface** — surface the 352 rows; price/performance (intelligence-vs-cost) frontier; \"best-for-X\" cards; sortable master table; junk-filter. *(NS1, NS2 — RESEARCH \"protect\" item; highest value-per-effort.)*\n57\t2. **Benchmark collection (thin slice)** — OpenRouter `/models` (specs/pricing) + Epoch AI CC-BY (GPQA/SWE-bench/FrontierMath); compute own composite; per-cell `source`/`as_of`/`self_reported`. *(NS2.)*\n58\t3. **Collection retargeting** — add high-signal agentic sources (HF Daily Papers, GitHub star-velocity, provider feeds, trusted aggregators) + a frontier-relevance ranker, **with a raw-arxiv recall safety net + authority-bypass lane + label-validated weights.** *(NS4.)*\n59\t4. **Adoption decision surface** — decision-card content (what/fit/recommendation+confidence/advantages/risks/provenance/effort), persisted decisions table feeding Helping Hand — **delivered primarily through the report**, not a heavy daily triage UI. *(NS3.)*\n60\t5. **Honest value + plain-English health** — RAG + 4-question summary; metric set with n shown and rates suppressed below n<30. *(NS5.)*\n61\t6. **Per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" awareness view** (momentum), promoting existing sweep deltas. *(NS1.)*\n62\t7. **Knowledge/relationship map** — LAST, OPTIONAL, **off the ingestion critical path**: PCA/TruncatedSVD + plain canvas (NOT UMAP/numba), non-authoritative. *(NS1 — down-weighted per RESEARCH §B.)*\n63\t\n64\t**OUT of scope (this run):** rebuilding the dashboard package or KB schema; a separate \"critical-analysis tool\" (your later session); any auto consensus \"ring\"; a swarm-harness AuroraTwo rebuild; live cloud viz services.\n65\t\n66\t**CONSTRAINED (hard rules, from you + RESEARCH §B — carried to every wave):**\n67\t- Dirty working tree **IS production**; changes are live. Real schedule 01:07–06:47.\n68\t- **Never** run the `migrate_to_kind_paper` delete step. **Never** read `.env`.\n69\t- KB is **read-only except** the new `decisions` / `feedback` (and benchmark/score) tables.\n70\t- OpenRouter = **transient enrichment**, not redistribution (ToS) — store derived facts, attribute, tolerate 401.\n71\t- **Per-row benchmark license metadata** (Epoch CC-BY; Aider/Terminal-Bench Apache-2.0; MMLU-Pro absent from Epoch).\n72\t- **No metric rate shown below n<30**; show raw counts; name the open-loop/bootstrap state.\n73\t- **UMAP/numba/llvmlite must NOT be on the nightly ingestion critical path** (isolate, or use PCA+canvas).\n74\t- `frontier_score` weights **validated against John's labeled liked/rejected finds** before any gate is trusted; authority-bypass lane preserves recall.\n75\t\n76\t---\n77\t\n78\t## 4. Inclusion test + Oranges foresight (receipt)\n79\t\n80\t**Inclusion test applied now:** the knowledge map (item 7) is the weakest North-Star server (RESEARCH: \"least decision-useful; same class John rejected\") — it survives only because John explicitly asked for it AND it's fenced to optional/off-critical-path. Everything else maps directly to NS1–NS5.\n81\t\n82\t**Oranges foresight (real-intent, 2-3 steps ahead):**\n83\t- **Real goal behind \"am I wasting a dollar a night?\"** is not a cost report — it's *trust that the spend buys awareness he'd otherwise miss.* So value-accounting (NS5) and right-collection (NS4) are load-bearing, not cosmetic.\n84\t- **Reorder receipt:** model-intelligence (already-paid-for data) is sequenced FIRST despite the handoff listing surfaces and collection co-equally — counterfactual cost of not doing so: we'd spend the first wave on collection plumbing while the highest-value, zero-new-data win keeps sitting invisible.\n85\t- **Dropped branch:** a daily keyboard-triage adoption queue — counterfactual cost: ~2 decisions/week don't justify a visit-me surface; mitigated by moving the decision into the report (where John already is), preserving the value while dropping the build.\n86\t- **Cross-cutting win surfaced early:** push value into the **morning report / a weekly email**, not new surfaces John must visit — this threads through NS1/NS3/NS5.\n87\t\n88\t---\n89\t\n90\t## 🚦 LOCK GATE — your decision\n91\t\n92\t**To proceed to Stage 1 (Master Plan), please confirm:**\n93\t\n94\t1. **Lock the North Star** in §1 (and its NS1–NS5 success criteria) as the frozen objective? (yes / edit)\n95\t2. **Scope §3** — anything to ADD, CUT, or move between IN / OUT / CONSTRAINED? (In particular: keep the knowledge map IN-but-optional, or cut it entirely this run?)\n96\t3. **Any constraint missing** from §3's hard-rules list?\n97\t\n98\tNothing downstream is planned until you lock. After the lock, Stage 1 runs the Oranges brainstorm + Shark-Tank loop to a phased Master Plan, presented to you verbatim.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp7xYPhNGPdp6bdeA6FWy","session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"9ff63bd2-9a7d-4b52-974d-9311536cb98b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:12:23.898Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace Aurora strategic trajectory"}
