{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HTBwQu6rGFkTQ4JFKaWNr2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora — Session handoff for a fresh Cowork session\n2\t\n3\t**Last updated:** 2026-05-18, end of the session that built Aurora P0–P8,\n4\tdiagnosed the overnight outage, hardened against future reboots, and\n5\tpublished the Helping Hand plugin to GitHub + installed it across runtimes.\n6\t\n7\tThis document is what a brand-new Cowork session should read first to pick up\n8\twhere this one left off.\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## What Aurora is, in one paragraph\n13\t\n14\tAurora is a nightly multi-agent system that sweeps GitHub / awesome-lists /\n15\tarXiv / RSS for new Claude **skills**, agent **tools**, and OSS agent\n16\t**frameworks**, validates them with a lite swarm (Sonnet runner +\n17\tSonnet critic_a + Gemini critic_b + reconciler), files them into a hierarchical\n18\tlibrary indexed by **domain × complexity**, and publishes a snapshot to a\n19\tGitHub repo so collaborators can install a **Helping Hand** plugin and get\n20\tin-session recommendations from the curated catalog.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Current state — 2026-05-18\n25\t\n26\t### Pipeline status\n27\t\n28\t| Sweep | Schedule | Last run (UTC) | Status | Cost | Filed |\n29\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n30\t| Skills  | 23:00 Mon–Sun | 2026-05-17 23:00 | ok | $0.1520 | 151 |\n31\t| Tools   | 00:00 daily   | 2026-05-18 00:00 | ok | $0.0678 |  85 |\n32\t| Agents  | 01:00 daily   | 2026-05-18 01:00 | ok | $0.0597 |  40 |\n33\t| Morning briefing + publish | 08:30 daily | 2026-05-18 08:30 | ok | n/a | — |\n34\t\n35\tLibrary totals: **39 skills, 0 templates, 241 tools, 55 agents.**\n36\tMTD spend: anthropic $0.71 / gemini $0.03 / local $0.00 (all caps OK).\n37\t\n38\t### Repo\n39\t\n40\t- `https://github.com/johncliechty/aurora-library` — `main` at commit\n41\t  `63d240f \"nightly 20260518\"`, tagged `20260518`. Last push log at\n42\t  `C:\\dev\\aurora\\_publish\\last_push.log`.\n43\t- `COLLABORATOR-SETUP.md` is the entry doc for anyone cloning the repo.\n44\t\n45\t### Helping Hand install state\n46\t\n47\t| Runtime | Install state | Path |\n48\t|---|---|---|\n49\t| Claude Code (user-level) | installed | `~/.claude/skills/helping-hand/`, `~/.claude/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/`, `~/.claude/.mcp.json` |\n50\t| Gemini CLI | descriptor installed; MCP best-effort | `~/.gemini/skills/helping-hand/` |\n51\t| Cowork | **plugin file shipped; install pending user** — drag `C:\\dev\\aurora\\helping-hand.plugin` into a Cowork chat |\n52\t\n53\t### Windows reboot configuration\n54\t\n55\t- Active Hours: **04:00–22:00** (registry-pinned via admin).\n56\t- `ScheduledInstallTime=3` (03:00) for Windows Update reboots — slotted between\n57\t  the 01:00 agents-sweep end and 04:00 active-hours start.\n58\t- All four Aurora scheduled tasks have `WakeToRun=True` and\n59\t  `StartWhenAvailable=True`.\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## What to pick up next\n64\t\n65\t### This-week punch list (curator-side — `C:\\dev\\aurora`)\n66\t\n67\t1. **Sunburst `library/_map.html`** — d3 sunburst, domain × complexity. ~80\n68\t   lines. Output goes into the publish tree.\n69\t2. **Neural-plasticity scoring** — populate `neural_plasticity` table for the\n70\t   55 agents (Haiku, ~$0.10). Plan §7 has the criteria.\n71\t3. **Template detection heuristic** in `roles/static_screener.py`. Right now\n72\t   nothing routes into `kind='template'` (the 4th artifact class) so the\n73\t   library template count stays at 0. Cheapest heuristic: front-matter\n74\t   `kind: template` OR README/title containing \"boilerplate\", \"starter\",\n75\t   \"scaffold\", \"cookbook\" with no `description:` skill block.\n76\t4. **Re-embed legacy URL-slug entries** that pre-date the fixture-slug fix.\n77\t   Look for `library/tools/c-dev-*` and `library/tools/*-skill-md` shaped\n78\t   slugs (they're fixture/path-derived, not project-derived).\n79\t5. **Critic B prompt tuning** — the Gemini critic is hitting MAX_TOKENS and\n80\t   falling back to Haiku more than it should. Trim the prompt or bump\n81\t   `max_output_tokens`.\n82\t6. **HH threshold calibration** — `HELPING_HAND_THRESHOLD=0.65` is the\n83\t   default. After a week of collaborator signal (acceptance vs. dismissal,\n84\t   logged in their local snapshots if they opt into `read_write` mode),\n85\t   revisit.\n86\t\n87\t### User-side (John)\n88\t\n89\t- Install Helping Hand for Cowork (drag .plugin into UI).\n90\t- Generate dedicated API keys (`aurora` Anthropic $50/mo, `aurora-critic-b`\n91\t  Gemini $10/mo), swap into `C:\\dev\\aurora\\.env`, then\n92\t  `New-Item C:\\dev\\aurora\\.keys-dedicated -ItemType File` to silence the\n93\t  morning nudge.\n94\t- Invite the first collaborator with the link to\n95\t  `https://github.com/johncliechty/aurora-library` and point them at\n96\t  `COLLABORATOR-SETUP.md`.\n97\t\n98\t### Deferred to its own session — GWL / OpenClaw integration\n99\t\n100\t**Don't try to do this here.** Plan §19 has the full scope but the short"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp7xYPhNGPdp6bdeA6FWy","session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"55a8995f-64e1-4603-a3a1-c133aff5cd19","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:12:26.736Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Trace Aurora strategic trajectory"}
