 is a new CLI/TUI agent for searching and downloading GIFs across multiple providers, with capabilities to extract still frames and contact sheets. **himalaya** expands email automation by providing IMAP/SMTP command-line access for mail operations (list, read, search, compose, reply, forward, copy, move, delete). **imsg** adds local macOS iMessage/SMS integration via Messages.app, enabling chat listing, history retrieval, and message sending through the CLI.\n33\t\n34\tThese additions reflect a consolidation trend around **communication and media retrieval tooling**. If you're building agents that need to integrate messaging (email, SMS, or iMessage), you now have dedicated CLI tools rather than relying on web APIs or native app automation. The gifgrep agent is particularly novel—it addresses a gap in programmatic GIF discovery and asset extraction. None of these tools appear in the neural plasticity matrix yet, so their learning/memory characteristics remain unverified. Consider these tools if your workflow involves automated message processing, GIF asset management, or hybrid communication channels (email + SMS + iMessage in one agent context). All three are available as skills under the openclaw project.\n35\t\n36\t## 💰 Pricing Watch — Verified Changes\n37\t\n38\t_Mode: **dry-run** · 28 row(s) considered_\n39\t\n40\t| Model | DB | Proposed | Status | Source |\n41\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n42\t| Google Gemini Flash Latest | $1.5/$9.0 | $1.5/$9.0 | 🔍 DRY-RUN (first-party, not applied) | https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing |\n43\t| Google: Gemini 2.5 Flash | $0.3/$2.5 | $0.3/$2.5 | 🔍 DRY-RUN (first-party, not applied) | https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing |\n44\t| Google: Gemini 2.5 Pro | $1.25/$10.0 | $1.25/$10.0 | 🔍 DRY-RUN (first-party, not applied) | https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing |\n45\t| Amazon: Nova 2 Lite | $0.3/$2.5 | $0.3/$2.5 | 🔍 DRY-RUN (aggregator-quorum, not applied) | https://openrouter.ai/models/amazon/nova-2-lite-v1