{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp7xYPhNGPdp6bdeA6FWy","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I now have a comprehensive understanding of Aurora's trajectory. Let me compile my findings.\n\n---\n\n## Aurora Strategic Trajectory — Comprehensive Report\n\n### ORIGINAL PROBLEM & CONCEPTION (May 2026)\n\n**Original problem statement** (from README.md:1-7):\n> \"Three nightly multi-agent sweeps that discover, validate, and catalog the open-source Claude/agent ecosystem — Skills & Templates (23:00), Tools (00:00), Agents (01:00). Outputs: a SQLite knowledge base, a browsable markdown library, nightly executive summaries, an 08:30 morning briefing, and a `helping-hand` plugin that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork or Claude Code session.\"\n\n**Original North Star (May 2026, NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:115-149):**\n> \"Three independent multi-agent sweeps run every night against the open-source ecosystem and produce a curated, queryable knowledge base.\"\n\n**The user:** John Liechty, a solo operator building agentic AI systems. Aurora was designed to keep him current on the ecosystem (skills, tools, agents, frameworks) and automatically surface relevant findings into his current work session via a \"Helping Hand\" plugin.\n\n**Original dual-axis conception** (NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:9, 673-692):\n- **What it does:** problem-domain hierarchy (autonomous systems, agent internals, memory/learning, etc.)\n- **How complex:** task-handling complexity (single-task, few-agent coordination, many-agent systems, etc.)\n\nThis reflected a sophisticated, research-first framing: Aurora would track the **neural-plasticity / learning / memory dimensions** of agent frameworks alongside functional capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### REFRAMING #1: JUNE 6, 2026 — \"Value + Architecture, Co-Equal\"\n\n**Crucible Stage 0 Lock (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:8-13, dated 2026-06-06):**\n\n> \"Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value** *and* run on a **robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture** — as **co-equal goals**. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine.\"\n\n**What changed in conception:**\n- **May 2026**: Aurora was a \"discovery engine\" optimized for breadth (sweeping the ecosystem systematically)\n- **June 6, 2026**: Reframed around **John's felt experience**. The adversarial Crucible review found that ~70% of the pain was an unwired \"consume loop\" (he wasn't actually *using* the outputs), not the discovery engine itself.\n\n**The \"thin-vertical-first\" wave decomposition (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:49-169):**\n\nThis reverses traditional priorities:\n1. **Wave 0**: Re-light Helping Hand (the consume bridge)\n2. **Wave 1**: Make output visible (briefing push, library index fix)\n3. **Wave 2**: Single-owner security gate + backfill\n4. **Wave 3**: **Evidence-rigor fix-loop → confidence badge** (the keystone)\n5. **Wave 4**: Trustworthy cost numbers\n6. **Wave 5**: Scout memory / source-reputation\n\n**Critical insight from June 6 doc (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-45):**\n> \"~70% of the felt pain is an unwired 'consume' loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine... Aurora's *produce* half works (889 artifacts, nightly briefings generated); the *consume* half was dead at every bridge.\"\n\n**Architecture decision:** NOT a Foreman-style swarm rebuild. Instead, the **Foreman/Crucible *pattern*** (fresh-context sub-agents + adversarial EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX) but **keep the serial discovery** because `TOP_K=2` makes judgment parallelism \"engineering theater\" (AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md:36-47 provides empirical funnel data: 82:1 ratio of static-screener to LLM reconciler across lifetime).\n\n---\n\n### REFRAMING #2: JUNE 9-11, 2026 — \"Agentic-AI Awareness Instrument\"\n\n**Discovery Quality Plan lock (AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:7-22, dated 2026-06-09):**\n\n> \"Objective: Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting, and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed, measurable value loop — **built by evolving the existing pipeline, never touching the proven plumbing.**\"\n\n**Success criteria re-articulated (6 numbered inclusion-test points):**\n1. Right kind at ingest (arxiv ≠ tool, no vendor blogspam)\n2. Top finds named, ranked, with \"why this matters\"\n3. Persisted taste score tuned to John's profile\n4. Value loop closes on real usage data\n5. Catalog is trustworthy (deduped, stale entries retire)\n6. Felt immediately, weekly thereafter\n\n**Then came the Awareness Revamp cascade (June 11, HANDOFF.md:1-59):**\n\nAfter John *used* the newly-built dashboard, the conception shifted again:\n\n**Verbatim from John's intent (HANDOFF.md:26-30, bolding original):**\n\n> \"Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools**. This serves THREE jobs, co-equal:\n> 1. **Educate John** — keep him current on the field.\n> 2. **Guide generation of new agents** — inform what he builds (GWL agents, etc.).\n> 3. **Feed the agentic systems** — make all of it available to the GWL agentic system, to Claude (via the **Helping Hand** skill), and to Gemini (via Helping Hand) for retrieval.\"\n\n**The specific pain points John articulated (HANDOFF.md:48-59, table):**\n\n| Reaction | Real ask |\n|---|---|\n| B: \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money\" | Honest value accounting: what did the spend buy? |\n| C: Suggested adoption — is this something I act on? | Make adoption actionable with human-readable summary, risks, advantages, recommendation |\n| D: \"Completely not helpful… looks like something a computer might read\" (on health page) | Human-readable health + value: plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about\" |\n| E: Want it by category + \"am I actually collecting anything?\" + models+pricing | Per-category intelligence surface: current best-in-class + newly notable + category-specific |\n| F: Not a taxonomy. Wants a knowledge/relationship map | How systems/harnesses/models/skills *relate*, emergent reasonable classifications |\n\n**The gap stated plainly (HANDOFF.md:93-109):**\n\n> \"Aurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an **agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**.\"\n\n**Grounded facts about what's misaligned (RESEARCH.md:9-22, EXECUTIVE SUMMARY):**\n\n- **352 priced models exist in the KB, surfaced nowhere** (highest-value asset, already paid-for)\n- **0 benchmarks collected** (John explicitly wants \"the benches\")\n- **Collection skewed to arxiv papers** (~8 papers/0 skills-tools-agents last night) — \"that's why 'nothing new' showed\"\n- **Taste/usage loop is thin:** `hh_events` has 106 events total but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 3 weeks\n- Verdict: **\"Not yet worth it / marginal, and drifting toward 'dies looking healthy'\"** — a self-healing, green-status machine feeding a database John doesn't open\n\n---\n\n### THE THROUGH-LINE ACROSS REFRAMINGS\n\n**What stayed constant:**\n- **The KB schema and SQLite are locked** (never rebuild from scratch — AuroraTwo verdict: EVOLUTION, NOT REWRITE)\n- **Security gating is locked** (single-owner gate predicate, deterministic cost telemetry)\n- **Helping Hand MCP as the consumer bridge** (though thresholds and filtering drifted)\n- **The seed maps and nightly schedule** (three sweeps, 23:00/00:00/01:00)\n\n**What shifted across three reframings:**\n\n| Dimension | May 2026 | June 6 | June 11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Primary goal** | Discover ecosystem breadth | John feels value + system runs robustly | John *becomes aware* (educate + guide-building + feed-agents) |\n| **Success measure** | Coverage (artifacts found, diverse sources) | Felt experience (briefing, library navigable, cost trusted) | Adoption decisions + honest value accounting + right collection |\n| **Value perception** | \"Keep John current\" (assumed he'd use it) | \"John sees outputs but doesn't use them; the consume bridge is broken\" | \"John doesn't trust what it finds; papers dominate, no models/benchmarks; can't decide what to adopt\" |\n| **Collection philosophy** | Broad, systematic sweep (arxiv, GitHub, awesome-lists) | Same, but better classified | **Frontier-relevant agentic-AI** (harnesses, models, benchmarks, high-signal skills) with **recall safety net** to avoid narrowing toward popularity-bias |\n| **Ranking/filtering** | Freshness + domain × complexity | Confidence badge + source quality | **Interest score (taste-scored)** + badge + kind-priority, with honest sample-size reporting |\n| **Delivery surface** | Library index + exec summaries | Visible briefing + Helping Hand | **Morning report + weekly email** (where John already lives); Helping Hand as retrieval for agents, not auto-push |\n\n---\n\n### EVIDENCE OF PIVOTING\n\n**Three distinct pivots detected:**\n\n1. **May → June 6 (\"Consume Loop Blocked\"):** The system *produced* correctly but *served* nothing. The fix was architectural (visibility + trust), not discovery-engine work. This pivot is driven by **empirical usage data** (Crucible's Shark-Tank found 70% of pain was unwired consume, not discovery quality).\n\n2. **June 6 → June 9 (\"Right Kind at Ingest\"):** Shift from \"surface more trustworthy finds\" to \"only collect and surface the *right* categories.\" This pivot is **quality-over-breadth** and is driven by the observation that arxiv papers dominate (8/night, never browsed) while the categories John cares about (skills, tools, agents, models, benchmarks) are underrepresented or missing.\n\n3. **June 9 → June 11 (\"Awareness + Decision Instrument\"):** The most significant reframing. Even *within* the right categories, the system was showing findings *passively* (raw lists) rather than *actively answering decisions* (which model for this task? should I adopt this tool?). The pivot is from **discovery-as-output** to **awareness-as-decision-making-support**. Driven by John's actual dashboard usage: \"tell me what's current best-in-class and why I should care.\"\n\n---\n\n### WHAT CHANGED ABOUT THE CONCEPTION OF VALUE\n\n**May 2026 value model:**\n- Value = breadth of discovery + research-quality metadata (neural-plasticity dimensions)\n- Metric: artifacts found, diverse sources, hierarchical placement\n- Failure mode: silently over-represents one source or author\n\n**June 6 value model:**\n- Value = felt value to John (he sees it, trusts it, uses it) + robust architecture\n- Metric: briefing pushed + library navigable + costs transparent + source quality visible\n- Failure mode: discovery engine is fine; the consume loop is broken\n\n**June 11 value model (Awareness Revamp, locked in Stage 0):**\n- **Value = John's *awareness* and *adoption decisions*** on what to build with / adopt / learn from\n- **Metrics (NS1–NS5 in STAGE0-FRAMING.md:21-35):**\n  - NS1: Per-category, \"current best-in-class + newly moved + why it matters\"\n  - NS2: Models + benchmarks surfaced + joined (decision-useful)\n  - NS3: Adoption decision (summary + risks + advantages + effort)\n  - NS4: **Right collection** (frontier-relevant without losing obscure small-author finds)\n  - NS5: Honest value (cost per useful find, sample sizes shown, rates suppressed when n<30)\n- Failure mode: beautiful green dashboard with zero actual usage (\"dies looking healthy\")\n\n**The stated \"honest verdict\" (RESEARCH.md:92-103):**\n> \"**Is Aurora worth running today? Not yet — marginal, and drifting the wrong way.** ... Of the three co-equal jobs — educate / guide agent-building / feed retrieval — it weakly does a fraction of #1 (paper awareness, only if John opens the dashboard) and essentially not #2 or #3.\"\n\n**3–5 changes that would make it genuinely valuable (ranked, RESEARCH.md:96-101):**\n1. **Surface the models table** (352 priced rows exist; highest value-per-effort)\n2. **Collect benchmarks** (thin slice: OpenRouter + Epoch AI)\n3. **Re-aim collection off arxiv toward harnesses/skills/tools**\n4. **Close the taste loop** (one-click rating in briefing; n=7 is too thin)\n5. **Make Helping Hand fire** (prove it with \"Aurora fed your sessions N times\")\n\n---\n\n### CURRENT STRATEGIC DIRECTION (June 23, 2026)\n\nThe project is **locked into the Awareness Revamp frame** with a **Stage 0 lock gate** (STAGE0-FRAMING.md:90-98):\n\n**North Star (locked verbatim, line 9-15):**\n> \"Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools** — serving THREE co-equal jobs: (1) **educate John**, (2) **guide his generation of new agents**, (3) **feed the agentic systems + Claude + Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.**\"\n\n**Scope locked (IN / OUT / CONSTRAINED):**\n\n**IN scope (serves NS1–NS5):**\n1. Model-intelligence surface (352 rows + price/perf frontier + best-for-X cards)\n2. Benchmark collection (OpenRouter + Epoch AI CC-BY)\n3. Collection retargeting (high-signal agentic sources + frontier-relevance ranker with recall safety net)\n4. Adoption decision surface (decision-cards in the report, not heavy triage UI)\n5. Honest value + plain-English health (RAG + 4-question summary, n-gated metrics)\n6. Per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" awareness\n7. Knowledge/relationship map (LAST, OPTIONAL, off critical path; PCA+canvas, NOT UMAP/numba)\n\n**Hard constraints** (from June 11 research validation):\n- Dirty working tree **IS production** (changes live immediately)\n- OpenRouter = **transient enrichment** (no redistribution; ToS forbids scraping)\n- **No metric rate shown below n<30**; show raw counts and name bootstrap problem\n- **UMAP/numba/llvmlite must NOT be on nightly ingestion critical path**\n- `frontier_score` weights **validated against John's labeled likes/rejects** before trusted\n\n**Cross-cutting win:** Push value into **morning report / weekly email**, not new surfaces John must visit.\n\n---\n\n### FINAL ASSESSMENT: THE NORTH STAR ARC\n\n**Thread across all three statements:**\n\n1. **May 2026**: \"Keep me aware of the agentic-AI ecosystem\" (implicit assumption: awareness = passive discovery)\n2. **June 6 2026**: \"Keep me aware AND make sure I actually use it\" (discovery + consume bridge)\n3. **June 11 2026**: \"Make me aware of what's worth adopting and why\" (discovery + trust + decision-support + agent-feeding)\n\nThe through-line is **awareness for action**, but the conception of what \"action\" means evolved:\n- May: passively browsing a library\n- June 6: actively using Helping Hand in sessions\n- June 11: **actively deciding what to adopt, build with, and learn from** — and Aurora feeding into his agents\n\n**Evidence of truth-seeking (not marketing):** The June 11 Awareness Revamp's research deliverable explicitly included a **\"blunt critique, no flattery\"** (HANDOFF.md:139-141) that concluded Aurora was **\"marginal and drifting the wrong way\"** despite the polished dashboard. This unflinching assessment — that self-healing can hide irrelevance — shaped the locked constraints (n-gating, honest sample sizes, explicit open-loop naming).\n\n**The most loaded concealed assumption:** The original May plan assumed John would *browse the library and exec summaries*. Every reframing discovered he doesn't — he lives in his morning report (Cowork session) and his editor (Claude Code). The June 11 \"cross-cutting win\" thus became architectural: **push all value into the report and Helping Hand, stop building surfaces John must visit.**\n\n---\n\n### REFERENCES\n\n**Locked North Stars (in order):**\n- **May 2026**: README.md:1-7, NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:115-149\n- **June 6 2026**: AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:8-13 (line 8-13)\n- **June 11 2026**: STAGE0-FRAMING.md:9-15 (explicitly locked as verbatim intent)\n\n**Critical pivot documents:**\n- AuroraTwo decision (June 6): `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md` — empirical funnel analysis, \"swarm is theater at TOP_K=2\"\n- Discovery Quality plan (June 9): `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:7-22` — \"right kind at ingest, smaller high-trust catalog\"\n- Awareness Revamp handoff (June 11): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md:1-59` — John's verbatim feedback post-dashboard\n- Blunt critique (June 11): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md:92-103` — \"not yet worth it, dies looking healthy\"\n- Current stage-0 frame (June 11): `docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/STAGE0-FRAMING.md:1-98` — locked north star + scope + constraints\n\n**Grounded evidence:**\n- Security/cost locked-in constraints: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:17-29`\n- Evidence of 70% pain being consume-loop: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-45`\n- Empirical funnel data (82:1 ratio): `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md:36-47`\n- Real hh_events usage (n=7 decisions in 3 weeks): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md:3` + `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:57` (E6)\n- Collection skew (8 papers/night, 0 skills-tools-agents): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md:62-69` (§3 Grounded Facts)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"c06edd13-3ce3-4ab9-a22f-90abd00861dd","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:13:41.785Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Aurora project docs at C:\\dev\\aurora to reconstruct its STRATEGIC TRAJECTORY — the sequence of reframings the project has gone through and where it is now pointed.\n\nRead these and report:\n1. docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md — the \"revamp\" North Star. What is the reframed objective? What are the \"waves\"? What does \"value+architecture co-equal, thin-vertical-first\" mean concretely?\n2. docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md (and any sibling files in that dir) — the LATEST direction: reframing Aurora as an \"agentic-AI awareness/decision instrument.\" What is the vision? What are the planned waves W1-W5+? What's done vs planned?\n3. docs/NOTES.md — recent working notes.\n4. README.md and CLAUDE.md — the stated purpose of Aurora.\n5. Any docs about the \"AuroraTwo decision\" (evolve vs rebuild) and the \"discovery quality plan.\"\n\nI want to understand: What problem does Aurora originally solve? Who is the user (looks like one person, John)? What is the through-line across the reframings, and what has CHANGED about the conception of value? Is there evidence of repeated pivoting? Quote the actual North Star / objective statements verbatim where you find them.\n\nReport with file:line references and verbatim quotes of objective/vision statements. Do not propose changes. Very thorough exploration.","agentId":"aefb1831d6e4ed381","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I now have a comprehensive understanding of Aurora's trajectory. Let me compile my findings.\n\n---\n\n## Aurora Strategic Trajectory — Comprehensive Report\n\n### ORIGINAL PROBLEM & CONCEPTION (May 2026)\n\n**Original problem statement** (from README.md:1-7):\n> \"Three nightly multi-agent sweeps that discover, validate, and catalog the open-source Claude/agent ecosystem — Skills & Templates (23:00), Tools (00:00), Agents (01:00). Outputs: a SQLite knowledge base, a browsable markdown library, nightly executive summaries, an 08:30 morning briefing, and a `helping-hand` plugin that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork or Claude Code session.\"\n\n**Original North Star (May 2026, NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:115-149):**\n> \"Three independent multi-agent sweeps run every night against the open-source ecosystem and produce a curated, queryable knowledge base.\"\n\n**The user:** John Liechty, a solo operator building agentic AI systems. Aurora was designed to keep him current on the ecosystem (skills, tools, agents, frameworks) and automatically surface relevant findings into his current work session via a \"Helping Hand\" plugin.\n\n**Original dual-axis conception** (NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:9, 673-692):\n- **What it does:** problem-domain hierarchy (autonomous systems, agent internals, memory/learning, etc.)\n- **How complex:** task-handling complexity (single-task, few-agent coordination, many-agent systems, etc.)\n\nThis reflected a sophisticated, research-first framing: Aurora would track the **neural-plasticity / learning / memory dimensions** of agent frameworks alongside functional capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### REFRAMING #1: JUNE 6, 2026 — \"Value + Architecture, Co-Equal\"\n\n**Crucible Stage 0 Lock (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:8-13, dated 2026-06-06):**\n\n> \"Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value** *and* run on a **robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture** — as **co-equal goals**. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine.\"\n\n**What changed in conception:**\n- **May 2026**: Aurora was a \"discovery engine\" optimized for breadth (sweeping the ecosystem systematically)\n- **June 6, 2026**: Reframed around **John's felt experience**. The adversarial Crucible review found that ~70% of the pain was an unwired \"consume loop\" (he wasn't actually *using* the outputs), not the discovery engine itself.\n\n**The \"thin-vertical-first\" wave decomposition (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:49-169):**\n\nThis reverses traditional priorities:\n1. **Wave 0**: Re-light Helping Hand (the consume bridge)\n2. **Wave 1**: Make output visible (briefing push, library index fix)\n3. **Wave 2**: Single-owner security gate + backfill\n4. **Wave 3**: **Evidence-rigor fix-loop → confidence badge** (the keystone)\n5. **Wave 4**: Trustworthy cost numbers\n6. **Wave 5**: Scout memory / source-reputation\n\n**Critical insight from June 6 doc (AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-45):**\n> \"~70% of the felt pain is an unwired 'consume' loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine... Aurora's *produce* half works (889 artifacts, nightly briefings generated); the *consume* half was dead at every bridge.\"\n\n**Architecture decision:** NOT a Foreman-style swarm rebuild. Instead, the **Foreman/Crucible *pattern*** (fresh-context sub-agents + adversarial EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX) but **keep the serial discovery** because `TOP_K=2` makes judgment parallelism \"engineering theater\" (AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md:36-47 provides empirical funnel data: 82:1 ratio of static-screener to LLM reconciler across lifetime).\n\n---\n\n### REFRAMING #2: JUNE 9-11, 2026 — \"Agentic-AI Awareness Instrument\"\n\n**Discovery Quality Plan lock (AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:7-22, dated 2026-06-09):**\n\n> \"Objective: Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting, and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed, measurable value loop — **built by evolving the existing pipeline, never touching the proven plumbing.**\"\n\n**Success criteria re-articulated (6 numbered inclusion-test points):**\n1. Right kind at ingest (arxiv ≠ tool, no vendor blogspam)\n2. Top finds named, ranked, with \"why this matters\"\n3. Persisted taste score tuned to John's profile\n4. Value loop closes on real usage data\n5. Catalog is trustworthy (deduped, stale entries retire)\n6. Felt immediately, weekly thereafter\n\n**Then came the Awareness Revamp cascade (June 11, HANDOFF.md:1-59):**\n\nAfter John *used* the newly-built dashboard, the conception shifted again:\n\n**Verbatim from John's intent (HANDOFF.md:26-30, bolding original):**\n\n> \"Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools**. This serves THREE jobs, co-equal:\n> 1. **Educate John** — keep him current on the field.\n> 2. **Guide generation of new agents** — inform what he builds (GWL agents, etc.).\n> 3. **Feed the agentic systems** — make all of it available to the GWL agentic system, to Claude (via the **Helping Hand** skill), and to Gemini (via Helping Hand) for retrieval.\"\n\n**The specific pain points John articulated (HANDOFF.md:48-59, table):**\n\n| Reaction | Real ask |\n|---|---|\n| B: \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money\" | Honest value accounting: what did the spend buy? |\n| C: Suggested adoption — is this something I act on? | Make adoption actionable with human-readable summary, risks, advantages, recommendation |\n| D: \"Completely not helpful… looks like something a computer might read\" (on health page) | Human-readable health + value: plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about\" |\n| E: Want it by category + \"am I actually collecting anything?\" + models+pricing | Per-category intelligence surface: current best-in-class + newly notable + category-specific |\n| F: Not a taxonomy. Wants a knowledge/relationship map | How systems/harnesses/models/skills *relate*, emergent reasonable classifications |\n\n**The gap stated plainly (HANDOFF.md:93-109):**\n\n> \"Aurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an **agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**.\"\n\n**Grounded facts about what's misaligned (RESEARCH.md:9-22, EXECUTIVE SUMMARY):**\n\n- **352 priced models exist in the KB, surfaced nowhere** (highest-value asset, already paid-for)\n- **0 benchmarks collected** (John explicitly wants \"the benches\")\n- **Collection skewed to arxiv papers** (~8 papers/0 skills-tools-agents last night) — \"that's why 'nothing new' showed\"\n- **Taste/usage loop is thin:** `hh_events` has 106 events total but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 3 weeks\n- Verdict: **\"Not yet worth it / marginal, and drifting toward 'dies looking healthy'\"** — a self-healing, green-status machine feeding a database John doesn't open\n\n---\n\n### THE THROUGH-LINE ACROSS REFRAMINGS\n\n**What stayed constant:**\n- **The KB schema and SQLite are locked** (never rebuild from scratch — AuroraTwo verdict: EVOLUTION, NOT REWRITE)\n- **Security gating is locked** (single-owner gate predicate, deterministic cost telemetry)\n- **Helping Hand MCP as the consumer bridge** (though thresholds and filtering drifted)\n- **The seed maps and nightly schedule** (three sweeps, 23:00/00:00/01:00)\n\n**What shifted across three reframings:**\n\n| Dimension | May 2026 | June 6 | June 11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Primary goal** | Discover ecosystem breadth | John feels value + system runs robustly | John *becomes aware* (educate + guide-building + feed-agents) |\n| **Success measure** | Coverage (artifacts found, diverse sources) | Felt experience (briefing, library navigable, cost trusted) | Adoption decisions + honest value accounting + right collection |\n| **Value perception** | \"Keep John current\" (assumed he'd use it) | \"John sees outputs but doesn't use them; the consume bridge is broken\" | \"John doesn't trust what it finds; papers dominate, no models/benchmarks; can't decide what to adopt\" |\n| **Collection philosophy** | Broad, systematic sweep (arxiv, GitHub, awesome-lists) | Same, but better classified | **Frontier-relevant agentic-AI** (harnesses, models, benchmarks, high-signal skills) with **recall safety net** to avoid narrowing toward popularity-bias |\n| **Ranking/filtering** | Freshness + domain × complexity | Confidence badge + source quality | **Interest score (taste-scored)** + badge + kind-priority, with honest sample-size reporting |\n| **Delivery surface** | Library index + exec summaries | Visible briefing + Helping Hand | **Morning report + weekly email** (where John already lives); Helping Hand as retrieval for agents, not auto-push |\n\n---\n\n### EVIDENCE OF PIVOTING\n\n**Three distinct pivots detected:**\n\n1. **May → June 6 (\"Consume Loop Blocked\"):** The system *produced* correctly but *served* nothing. The fix was architectural (visibility + trust), not discovery-engine work. This pivot is driven by **empirical usage data** (Crucible's Shark-Tank found 70% of pain was unwired consume, not discovery quality).\n\n2. **June 6 → June 9 (\"Right Kind at Ingest\"):** Shift from \"surface more trustworthy finds\" to \"only collect and surface the *right* categories.\" This pivot is **quality-over-breadth** and is driven by the observation that arxiv papers dominate (8/night, never browsed) while the categories John cares about (skills, tools, agents, models, benchmarks) are underrepresented or missing.\n\n3. **June 9 → June 11 (\"Awareness + Decision Instrument\"):** The most significant reframing. Even *within* the right categories, the system was showing findings *passively* (raw lists) rather than *actively answering decisions* (which model for this task? should I adopt this tool?). The pivot is from **discovery-as-output** to **awareness-as-decision-making-support**. Driven by John's actual dashboard usage: \"tell me what's current best-in-class and why I should care.\"\n\n---\n\n### WHAT CHANGED ABOUT THE CONCEPTION OF VALUE\n\n**May 2026 value model:**\n- Value = breadth of discovery + research-quality metadata (neural-plasticity dimensions)\n- Metric: artifacts found, diverse sources, hierarchical placement\n- Failure mode: silently over-represents one source or author\n\n**June 6 value model:**\n- Value = felt value to John (he sees it, trusts it, uses it) + robust architecture\n- Metric: briefing pushed + library navigable + costs transparent + source quality visible\n- Failure mode: discovery engine is fine; the consume loop is broken\n\n**June 11 value model (Awareness Revamp, locked in Stage 0):**\n- **Value = John's *awareness* and *adoption decisions*** on what to build with / adopt / learn from\n- **Metrics (NS1–NS5 in STAGE0-FRAMING.md:21-35):**\n  - NS1: Per-category, \"current best-in-class + newly moved + why it matters\"\n  - NS2: Models + benchmarks surfaced + joined (decision-useful)\n  - NS3: Adoption decision (summary + risks + advantages + effort)\n  - NS4: **Right collection** (frontier-relevant without losing obscure small-author finds)\n  - NS5: Honest value (cost per useful find, sample sizes shown, rates suppressed when n<30)\n- Failure mode: beautiful green dashboard with zero actual usage (\"dies looking healthy\")\n\n**The stated \"honest verdict\" (RESEARCH.md:92-103):**\n> \"**Is Aurora worth running today? Not yet — marginal, and drifting the wrong way.** ... Of the three co-equal jobs — educate / guide agent-building / feed retrieval — it weakly does a fraction of #1 (paper awareness, only if John opens the dashboard) and essentially not #2 or #3.\"\n\n**3–5 changes that would make it genuinely valuable (ranked, RESEARCH.md:96-101):**\n1. **Surface the models table** (352 priced rows exist; highest value-per-effort)\n2. **Collect benchmarks** (thin slice: OpenRouter + Epoch AI)\n3. **Re-aim collection off arxiv toward harnesses/skills/tools**\n4. **Close the taste loop** (one-click rating in briefing; n=7 is too thin)\n5. **Make Helping Hand fire** (prove it with \"Aurora fed your sessions N times\")\n\n---\n\n### CURRENT STRATEGIC DIRECTION (June 23, 2026)\n\nThe project is **locked into the Awareness Revamp frame** with a **Stage 0 lock gate** (STAGE0-FRAMING.md:90-98):\n\n**North Star (locked verbatim, line 9-15):**\n> \"Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools** — serving THREE co-equal jobs: (1) **educate John**, (2) **guide his generation of new agents**, (3) **feed the agentic systems + Claude + Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.**\"\n\n**Scope locked (IN / OUT / CONSTRAINED):**\n\n**IN scope (serves NS1–NS5):**\n1. Model-intelligence surface (352 rows + price/perf frontier + best-for-X cards)\n2. Benchmark collection (OpenRouter + Epoch AI CC-BY)\n3. Collection retargeting (high-signal agentic sources + frontier-relevance ranker with recall safety net)\n4. Adoption decision surface (decision-cards in the report, not heavy triage UI)\n5. Honest value + plain-English health (RAG + 4-question summary, n-gated metrics)\n6. Per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" awareness\n7. Knowledge/relationship map (LAST, OPTIONAL, off critical path; PCA+canvas, NOT UMAP/numba)\n\n**Hard constraints** (from June 11 research validation):\n- Dirty working tree **IS production** (changes live immediately)\n- OpenRouter = **transient enrichment** (no redistribution; ToS forbids scraping)\n- **No metric rate shown below n<30**; show raw counts and name bootstrap problem\n- **UMAP/numba/llvmlite must NOT be on nightly ingestion critical path**\n- `frontier_score` weights **validated against John's labeled likes/rejects** before trusted\n\n**Cross-cutting win:** Push value into **morning report / weekly email**, not new surfaces John must visit.\n\n---\n\n### FINAL ASSESSMENT: THE NORTH STAR ARC\n\n**Thread across all three statements:**\n\n1. **May 2026**: \"Keep me aware of the agentic-AI ecosystem\" (implicit assumption: awareness = passive discovery)\n2. **June 6 2026**: \"Keep me aware AND make sure I actually use it\" (discovery + consume bridge)\n3. **June 11 2026**: \"Make me aware of what's worth adopting and why\" (discovery + trust + decision-support + agent-feeding)\n\nThe through-line is **awareness for action**, but the conception of what \"action\" means evolved:\n- May: passively browsing a library\n- June 6: actively using Helping Hand in sessions\n- June 11: **actively deciding what to adopt, build with, and learn from** — and Aurora feeding into his agents\n\n**Evidence of truth-seeking (not marketing):** The June 11 Awareness Revamp's research deliverable explicitly included a **\"blunt critique, no flattery\"** (HANDOFF.md:139-141) that concluded Aurora was **\"marginal and drifting the wrong way\"** despite the polished dashboard. This unflinching assessment — that self-healing can hide irrelevance — shaped the locked constraints (n-gating, honest sample sizes, explicit open-loop naming).\n\n**The most loaded concealed assumption:** The original May plan assumed John would *browse the library and exec summaries*. Every reframing discovered he doesn't — he lives in his morning report (Cowork session) and his editor (Claude Code). The June 11 \"cross-cutting win\" thus became architectural: **push all value into the report and Helping Hand, stop building surfaces John must visit.**\n\n---\n\n### REFERENCES\n\n**Locked North Stars (in order):**\n- **May 2026**: README.md:1-7, NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md:115-149\n- **June 6 2026**: AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:8-13 (line 8-13)\n- **June 11 2026**: STAGE0-FRAMING.md:9-15 (explicitly locked as verbatim intent)\n\n**Critical pivot documents:**\n- AuroraTwo decision (June 6): `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md` — empirical funnel analysis, \"swarm is theater at TOP_K=2\"\n- Discovery Quality plan (June 9): `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:7-22` — \"right kind at ingest, smaller high-trust catalog\"\n- Awareness Revamp handoff (June 11): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md:1-59` — John's verbatim feedback post-dashboard\n- Blunt critique (June 11): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md:92-103` — \"not yet worth it, dies looking healthy\"\n- Current stage-0 frame (June 11): `docs/foreman-handoff-awareness/STAGE0-FRAMING.md:1-98` — locked north star + scope + constraints\n\n**Grounded evidence:**\n- Security/cost locked-in constraints: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:17-29`\n- Evidence of 70% pain being consume-loop: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:35-45`\n- Empirical funnel data (82:1 ratio): `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md:36-47`\n- Real hh_events usage (n=7 decisions in 3 weeks): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md:3` + `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md:57` (E6)\n- Collection skew (8 papers/night, 0 skills-tools-agents): `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md:62-69` (§3 Grounded Facts)"}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":86589,"totalTokens":61638,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6726,"cache_read_input_tokens":50075,"output_tokens":4831,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6726},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4831,"cache_read_input_tokens":50075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6726,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":11,"searchCount":5,"bashCount":2,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
