-diligence, academic-verify are all positioned as trial recommendations.\n\n5. **Hands-off operation:** Nightly sweeps run autonomously on a Windows Scheduled Task without human intervention. System recovers from missed windows (WakeToRun, StartWhenAvailable, RestartCount=2).\n\n---\n\n### Bottom Line\n\n**Aurora is operationally real, not scaffolding.** It:\n- Runs 7+ scheduled tasks nightly, executing 100–400+ API calls per sweep\n- Grows a 34.5 MB knowledge base daily with 5–7 new artifacts\n- Generates auditable morning briefings (JSON + markdown + DOCX + PDF) with cost, quality, and catalog telemetry\n- Tracks $22/month spend against $50 monthly budget with honest open-loop value accounting\n- Surfaces a curated top-5 recommendations daily to the user via Helping Hand plugin\n- Maintains 590 browsable library artifacts with verified quality badges and security assessments\n\nThe system is **actively delivering value at $0.70–$1.00 per nightly run**, with the curator explicitly acknowledging the bootstrap phase (n<30 decisions needed before ranker weights can be trusted). This is honest, incremental value—not a complete solution, but a working artifact discovery + curation engine under active development."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"56e4149f-4f75-4608-b9dd-f28d7be69908","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:13:46.113Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Aurora project at C:\\dev\\aurora to assess its OPERATIONAL REALITY — is this thing actually running and producing value, or is it mostly scaffolding?\n\nInvestigate and report:\n1. reports/ — especially reports/morning/latest_summary.json and any recent reports. What do the most recent outputs actually contain? Real data or empty? Quote the actual JSON content of latest_summary.json (it's safe — no secrets) including any \"session_note\", \"top_finds\", \"Productivity Index\", cost rollups.\n2. library/ — the browsable catalog. How m