{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VLkraJFgEdSF3EAkXiHTtu","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create the final report:\n\n## Aurora Project: Code Architecture Map\n\n**Summary**: Aurora is a mature, production-quality nightly multi-agent sweep system (3 runs/day @ ~$0.56/sweep budget) that discovers, validates, and catalogs 350+ Claude skills, templates, tools, and open-source agents. The system is **fully built** with concrete implementations, not aspirational — deployment-ready with cost controls, security gates, and comprehensive testing.\n\n---\n\n### 1. ORCHESTRATOR PIPELINE\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/orchestrator.py` (1,456 lines)  \n**Entry Point**: `python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep {skills|tools|agents|models}`\n\n#### Sweep Modes\n- `--sweep skills` — Primary sweep covering Claude skills (typical nightly)\n- `--sweep tools` — MCP tools and other integrations\n- `--sweep agents` — Agent frameworks and autonomous systems\n- `--sweep models` — LLM model cards + benchmarks (separate pipeline)\n\n#### Execution Pipeline: Discover → Validate → Catalog\n\n**Main Walk (skills/tools/agents)** — orchestrator.walk_pipeline() [line 614]:\n\n1. **[1/8] Scout** (fetch phase)\n   - reads seed_map/{skills|tools|agents}.yaml (curated source URLs)\n   - Supports: local_mount, GitHub repos, RSS feeds, arXiv, awesome-lists, topic crawls\n   - Async per-host 1 req/sec throttle; respects AURORA_MAX_FETCH\n   - Yields ~50-200 FetchedSource objects per sweep\n\n2. **[2/8] Quarantine** (sanitization boundary)\n   - Wraps HTML/untrusted content with `<untrusted source=...>` markers\n   - Strips zero-width characters (injection defense)\n\n3. **[3.5/8] Sanitizer** (injection scrubbing)\n   - PromptArmor-style cheap-Haiku pass: detects prompt-injection patterns\n   - Fail-OPEN: outage never blocks sweep\n   - Records per-run injection count for telemetry\n\n4. **[4/8] Static Screener** (metadata-only qualification)\n   - Rejects: duplicates, broken links, pointer-only README links\n   - Returns ScannedCandidate with static_score (0..1)\n\n5. **[5/8] Split** (swarm vs. static-only routing)\n   - Top-K (default 2, env: AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K) → swarm (runner + 3 critics)\n   - Rest → static-only (embedder + librarian, no swarm)\n\n6. **[6/8] Swarm Path** (execution + multi-critic consensus) — for top-K only\n   - **Runner**: LLM-powered static analysis → {triggers, inputs, outputs, tool_surface, red_flags} artifact bundle (UUID-delimited to prevent injection)\n   - **Critic A** (Anthropic Sonnet 4.6, default): security + correctness skeptic on artifacts\n   - **Critic B** (Gemini 3.5-flash, default): quality + clarity evaluator\n   - **Critic C** (third-family judge: DeepSeek/Groq/Ollama, opt-in): cross-family consensus\n   - **Reconciler** (Anthropic Sonnet 4.6): fuses 2-3 verdicts → single pass/flag/reject\n   - **Evidence Loop** (Wave 3, SHADOW-default): iterative rigor via precomputed score function (zero LLM cost unless AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=1)\n   - Per-candidate budget check after each role; abort if PER_SWEEP_BUDGET exceeded\n\n7. **[7/8] Static Path** (embed + file, skip swarm)\n   - Embedder (Gemini 3.5-flash): places in 2D taxonomy (domain × complexity)\n   - Librarian: upserts artifact row, writes library/*.md\n\n8. **[8/8] Synthesis**\n   - Advisor (Wave-C): literature review → daily_syntheses + citation-grounded decision trees\n\n#### Budget Architecture\n\n**Per-sweep cap** [orchestrator.py:62]: $0.56 USD (50/30/3 = $50 monthly / 30 days / 3 sweeps)\n\n**Per-role budget cells** [lines 66-95] — sum < sweep_cap:\n- scout: 5%, sanitizer: 10%, runner: 35%, critic_a: 15%, critic_b: 15%, critic_c: 5%, reconciler: 10%, evidence_shadow: 10%, ranker_shadow: 8%, etc.\n- Pre-candidate + post-candidate checks via `_sweep_cost_so_far()`; exceeding any cell triggers `status='partial'`\n\n#### Shadow Features\n\n- **--retarget-shadow** (Wave 2): run high-signal sources + frontier ranker SHADOW-ONLY (never touch live KB)\n- **--dry-run**: walk pipeline with zero LLM calls, no network fetches\n- **--no-swarm**: skip runner+critics, embed/file all candidates (P2 mode)\n\n#### Models Sweep Pipeline\n\nSeparate walk_models_pipeline() [line ~1100]: smoke_runner (1-token live call per provider) → model_card_parser → screener → librarian → benchmarks ingest\n\n---\n\n### 2. LLM WRAPPER: llm.py\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/llm.py` (1,625 lines)\n\n#### Central LLM Call Funnels\n\n**call_anthropic()** [line 546]\n- Model default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (if unspecified; most roles override via env)\n- Retry: G1 bucket — tenacity full-jitter exponential 1..60s, 5 attempts, wall-clock 60s max\n- Transient error classifiers: timeouts, connection drops, 429/5xx/529 (NOT 4xx like 400/401/403)\n- **Sonnet → Haiku fallback**: on retryable Sonnet exhaustion, degrade once to Haiku (180s total wall-clock via HAIKU_FALLBACK_DEADLINE_S)\n- **Degrade counter**: per-run _DEGRADE_COUNT bumped on fallback; orchestrator checks post-walk (degrades → status='partial')\n\n**Wave L1 (Prompt Caching)** [line 151-396]\n- Gated by MODEL_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS per model (Sonnet 4.6 = 2048 tokens)\n- cache_prefix_clears_minimum() prevents silent no-ops below threshold\n- cache_read_tokens priced ~0.1x input, cache_write_tokens ~1.25x input\n- CostRecorder.record() accepts cache_read_tokens / cache_write_tokens separately\n\n**Wave L2 (System Prefix Caching)** [line 677]\n- When cache_system=True + system prefix ≥ min threshold, wraps in structured block with ephemeral cache_control\n- Fallback (Sonnet→Haiku) reuses same `kw`, so degraded Haiku still benefits\n\n**Wave L3 (Structured Outputs)** [line 638-651]\n- Forced strict tool use: one tool (_STRUCTURED_TOOL_NAME = \"emit_result\") whose input_schema IS the caller's output_schema\n- model.messages.create() with tool_choice + strict:true → schema-guaranteed JSON\n- Degrade path: on schema rejection after Sonnet→Haiku exhaustion, retry ONCE as plain text (legacy parse path)\n- Cost: metered ONCE off whichever call succeeded\n\n**Wave L4 (Adaptive Thinking)** [line 652-662]\n- When effort={low|medium|high|xhigh|max}, request carries thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"} + output_config={\"effort\": effort}\n- NEVER budget_tokens (deprecated on 4.6+, removed on Opus 4.7/4.8 → 400)\n- _assert_no_budget_tokens() guard at dispatch funnel\n- Thinking tokens folded into metered output via _fold_thinking_into_output()\n\n**call_gemini()** [line 1053]\n- Model default: gemini-3.5-flash\n- Falls back to Anthropic Haiku if GEMINI_API_KEY unset, AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI=1, or AURORA_CRITIC_B_PROVIDER=local\n- thinking_config={\"thinking_budget\": 0} to disable hidden thinking (cost-audit fix for May $118 incident)\n- Fold thoughts_token_count into metered tokens_out (Google bills at output rate)\n\n**call_gemini_embedding()** [line 1136]\n- Model: models/gemini-embedding-2 (Wave I1 migration from Voyage, 10x cheaper)\n- Returns [] gracefully on missing API key or disabled flag\n\n**call_model()** [line 1179]\n- Unified dispatcher: routes to call_anthropic or call_gemini based on model ID\n- Wave L2/L3/L4: cache_system/output_schema/effort only honored on Anthropic path\n- Gemini path ignores schema (keeps free-form text response)\n\n#### Cost Recording: CostRecorder [line 257]\n\n```python\nclass CostRecorder:\n    def record(self, vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out,\n               cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0,\n               batch_mode=False) -> float:  # returns USD estimate\n```\n\n- Writes one row to `costs` table per call\n- Pricing loaded from kb/pricing.yaml (lookup_rates function)\n- Wave L1: cache tokens priced at sub-rates (cache_read ~0.1x, cache_write ~1.25x)\n- Wave L6: batch_mode=True applies 0.5x discount (Message Batches API)\n- Legacy 4-arg path (vendor, model, tin, tout) is byte-for-byte pre-Wave-L1\n\n#### Pricing Substrate\n\n**kb/pricing.yaml** structure:\n```yaml\nbatch_discount: 0.5\nvendors:\n  anthropic:\n    claude-sonnet-4-6:\n      tokens_in_per_million_usd: 3.0\n      tokens_out_per_million_usd: 15.0\n      cache_read_per_million_usd: 0.3\n      cache_write_per_million_usd: 3.75\n    # ...Haiku 4.5, Opus 4.6/4.8, with tokenizer_factor: 1.35 for 4.8\n  gemini:\n    gemini-3.5-flash: [rates + verified:false flag]\n    gemini-embedding-2: [rates + verified:false flag]\n    # ...Gemini 2.5-pro/flash, text-embedding-004\n  deepseek:\n    deepseek-chat: [0.27 in / 1.10 out]\n  groq:\n    llama-3.3-70b-versatile: [0.59 in / 0.79 out]\n  local:\n    default: [0.0 / 0.0]\n```\n\n**lookup_rates()** [line 108]: returns (in_per_million, out_per_million) with warn-once on missing  \n**tokenizer_factor()** [line 183]: 1.35 for Opus 4.8 (pre-call estimates only, never metered)  \n**batch_discount()** [line 247]: 0.5 top-level multiplier\n\n#### Batch API (Wave L6)\n\n**submit_anthropic_batch()** [line ~900]\n- Collects {slug → critic_a_prompt} into ONE Batches API submission\n- Polls with exponential backoff until all items succeed/failed/canceled\n- Per-item failure degrades to synchronous (stored in _ca_batch_texts dict, empty for failures)\n- Cost metered at 0.5x via batch_mode=True\n\n---\n\n### 3. PUBLISHER: publisher.py\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/publisher.py` (857 lines)\n\n**Lifecycle**: runs nightly after agents sweep (01:45 UTC daily per plan §16.2)\n\n#### Build → Push Workflow\n\n1. **Snapshot creation** (kb-snapshot.sqlite)\n   - Copies aurora.db → staging kb-snapshot.sqlite\n   - Scrubs transcripts, artifact bundles (private sweep data)\n   - Applies security gate: only CLEAN artifacts (security_status='CLEAN') persisted\n   - Deletes benchmark rows with null/non-allowed licenses or restricted sources (AA/OpenRouter)\n   - Runs VACUUM to compact\n\n2. **CHANGELOG generation**\n   - Derives daily entry from today's successful run (run.status != 'failed')\n   - Rolls up metrics: {fetched, screened, placed, flagged, usd_estimate}\n\n3. **Staging tree** (PUBLISH_ROOT = _publish/)\n   - Explicit allowlist: seed_maps, reports/, certain library/ dirs\n   - Filters library/{kind}/{slug}/ via _artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot() predicate\n   - Copies only CLEAN + non-retired artifacts\n\n4. **Git commit + push** (if not --dry-run)\n   - Requires GITHUB_PAT + GITHUB_REPO in .env\n   - Tags with YYYYMMDD, pushes to aurora-library repo\n   - Stores PAT lifecycle + last push metadata in publisher_state table\n\n#### Disposition Matrix\n\n- **Artifacts table** → SHIP (applies security gate enforcement §4.2)\n- **model_benchmarks** → PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER (scrub non-allowed)\n- **Transcripts, artifact bundles** → SCRUB (never ship)\n- **ranking_diffs** → SCRUB (internal diagnostics)\n- **hh_events / hh_sessions** → SHIP (user-facing telemetry)\n\n---\n\n### 4. KNOWLEDGE BASE: kb/aurora.db\n\n**Schema**: v3 (kb/schema.sql, 29,368 bytes)\n\n#### Core Tables (9 + satellites)\n\n1. **artifacts** (primary, ~356 rows)\n   - Fields: sweep, kind, slug, name, short_description, canonical_url, github_full_name, license, language\n   - Security (Wave C): security_status, security_scanned_arf_version, payload_sha256\n   - Embeddings (I1): description_vec (gemini-embedding-2 LE float32)\n   - Taste (Wave 4): interest_score, interest_why, interest_scored_at\n   - Frontier (W2): frontier_score (Wave 2, SHADOW-only)\n   - First_seen_at, last_verified_at, last_surfaced_in_summary_at, retired_at\n   - Index: kind, canonical_url, security_status\n   - UNIQUE(sweep, slug)\n\n2. **aliases** (URL deduplication)\n   - artifact_id, observed_url (UNIQUE), first_observed_at\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n3. **sources** (provenance per-doc)\n   - artifact_id, url, curator, kind, fetched_at, content_sha256\n   - Wave B3: excerpt, title, extraction_offsets (JSON {field: [start, end]})\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n4. **runs** (nightly sweeps)\n   - sweep (skills|tools|agents|models), started_at, finished_at, status\n   - budget_tokens_in, budget_tokens_out\n   - seed_map_snapshot (BLOB), prompt_template_shas (JSON), model_ids (JSON)\n   - critic_c_status, critic_c_calls, critic_c_errors\n   - Wave 1: sanitizer_n_injections\n   - Index: (sweep, started_at)\n\n5. **validations** (per-candidate eval)\n   - artifact_id, run_id, stage (screener|runner|critic_a|critic_b|critic_c|reconciler), verdict, score, rationale\n   - transcript_path, artifact_bundle_path\n   - Index: artifact_id, run_id\n\n6. **costs** (per-call metering)\n   - run_id, role, vendor, model_id, tokens_in, tokens_out, usd_estimate, recorded_at\n   - Wave L1: cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens (NULL on legacy 4-arg calls)\n   - batch_mode (1 = Message Batch)\n   - Index: run_id, (vendor, recorded_at)\n   - **Powers**: exec_summary.py MTD rollups, morning_briefing cost tables\n\n7. **embeddings** (2D taxonomy placement)\n   - artifact_id, domain_path, domain_depth, complexity_rank (0..4), embedded_at\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n8. **neural_plasticity** (agents learning mechanics)\n   - artifact_id (PK), what_learns, learning_signal, what_is_modified, loss_or_objective, memory_model, etc.\n   - last_updated_at\n\n9. **hh_sessions / hh_events** (Helping Hand telemetry, Wave 3.2)\n   - hh_sessions: session_id, started_at, last_seen_at, scorer, match_calls\n   - hh_events: session_id, query_sha256, slug, artifact_kind, score, outcome, recorded_at\n   - Index: recorded_at, slug, session_id\n\n10. **models / model_benchmarks / model_smoke_tests** (Models sweep, v3.3)\n    - models: artifact_id, provider, family, version, context_in_tokens, max_output_tokens, pricing, etc.\n    - model_benchmarks: artifact_id, benchmark, score, source, license (CC3: PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER)\n    - model_smoke_tests: artifact_id, run_id, latency_ms, tokens, usd_estimate, error_msg\n\n11. **tool_install** (Wave A3 satellite)\n    - artifact_id (PK), install_method (npm|pip|cargo|...), invocation_kind (mcp-stdio|cli|...), mcp_config_json, etc.\n\n12. **Miscellaneous**: publisher_state, hh_interaction_buffer, hh_skill_upgrades, ranking_diffs (shadow)\n\n**Migrations**: kb/migrations/ directory (idempotent .sql files 0001-0027), applied at startup via kb.migrate\n\n---\n\n### 5. DASHBOARD: dashboard/ (Flask read-only)\n\n**Launch**: `python aurora_dashboard.py` → http://127.0.0.1:5001\n\n**Architecture**: Two-layer separation\n- `dashboard.data`: Flask-agnostic data layer (kb read-only, reports file reader) — imports ZERO aurora sweep code\n- `dashboard.web`: Flask blueprint factory over data layer → mountable on Anchor\n\n#### Data Layer (dashboard/data/, ~1,323 LOC)\n\n**Modules**:\n- **catalog.py**: artifact search, filter, detail (tags, aliases, sources, validations)\n- **costs.py**: cost rollups per-role, per-vendor, MTD tracking\n- **health.py**: run_status, noise_summary, degradation counts, rejects, log tails\n- **freshness.py**: fingerprint for change detection (poll optimization)\n- **models.py**: model cards, benchmark table, smoke test results\n- **reports.py**: file-based reports (decisions, state-reports, diffs)\n- **db.py**: read-only sqlite connection factory\n\n#### API Routes (blueprint.py, 13,774 bytes)\n\n- `/api/health` — liveness + full health object (runs, degradation, noise, backfills, logs)\n- `/api/health/summary` — human-readable alerts + signals (W4, never 500s)\n- `/api/health/detail?kind={noise|log|rejects|backfill}` — drill-down per signal\n- `/api/fingerprint` — hash for change detection\n- `/api/state` — machine state (seed maps, artifact counts by kind)\n- `/api/sweeps` — recent run list (W4)\n- `/api/sweep/{kind}/{date}` — detail for one sweep\n- `/api/morning` — morning briefing section (W2)\n- `/api/catalog/...` — artifact search, catalog stats (W5)\n- `/dashboard-static/*` — HTML/CSS/JS serving\n\n#### Static Assets (dashboard/web/static/)\n- dashboard.html — SPA entry point\n- Modern JS framework (observes /api/fingerprint for live polling)\n\n---\n\n### 6. DEPENDENCY SURFACE\n\n**pyproject.toml** — 52 direct dependencies:\n\n**Core Agents & LLM**:\n- claude-agent-sdk ≥0.1.81\n- anthropic ≥0.40\n- google-generativeai ≥0.8\n- openai ≥1.40 (local OpenAI-compatible fallback)\n\n**Async & Network**:\n- httpx ≥0.27 (async HTTP)\n- feedparser ≥6.0 (RSS)\n- tenacity ≥8.2 (retry with full-jitter)\n\n**Data & Config**:\n- pyyaml ≥6.0\n- pydantic ≥2.5\n- sqlite-utils ≥3.36\n- python-dotenv ≥1.0\n\n**Numerical**:\n- numpy ≥1.26\n- scikit-learn ≥1.4 (taxonomy placement)\n\n**Publishing & Reports**:\n- PyGithub ≥2.3 (git push)\n- reportlab ≥4.0 (PDF render, unicode-safe)\n- python-docx ≥1.0 (DOCX export)\n- fpdf2 ≥2.7 (legacy fallback)\n\n**Security & Extraction**:\n- detect-secrets ≥1.5 (secret scanning fallback)\n- langextract ≥1.2.0 (Google LangExtract adapter, soft-import, optional)\n\n**Dev**:\n- pytest ≥8.0, pytest-asyncio ≥0.23, ruff ≥0.5, mypy ≥1.10\n\n---\n\n### 7. CODE METRICS\n\n| Dimension | Count |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Total Python modules (excl. .venv) | 224 |\n| Top-level modules (orchestrator, llm, publisher, briefing_delivery, morning_briefing, exec_summary) | 6 |\n| **orchestrator.py** | 1,456 LOC |\n| **llm.py** | 1,625 LOC |\n| **publisher.py** | 857 LOC |\n| **morning_briefing.py** | 2,443 LOC |\n| Roles (roles/*.py) | 58 files, 13,574 LOC |\n| Security roles (roles/security/*.py) | 11 files, 4,855 LOC |\n| Dashboard data (dashboard/data/*.py) | 7 files, 1,323 LOC |\n| Test suite (tests/test_*.py) | **96 test files** |\n| KB migrations (kb/migrations/*.sql) | ~27 idempotent versions |\n\n---\n\n### 8. TEST COVERAGE\n\n**96 test files** covering:\n- **orchestrator**: walk_pipeline, budget cells, degrade counter, evidence loop, swarm/static split\n- **llm.py**: retry logic, cache gating, structured outputs, effort levels, batch API, degrade fallbacks\n- **publisher**: snapshot scrubbing, license filter, security gate, git push\n- **dashboard**: health signals, catalog queries, cost rollups, freshness\n- **roles**: scout, runner, critics, reconciler, sanitizer, quarantine, librarian, embedder, taste, advisor, evidence\n- **security**: ARF detector suite (AST rules, behavioral, regex, provenance), gate enforcement, sandbox confirmer\n- **models**: smoke testing, benchmarks, card parsing\n- **Helping Hand**: auto-mode, interaction buffer, session telemetry\n\nExamples: test_critic_c_cost.py, test_cost_cache_batch.py, test_per_role_budget.py, test_prompt_caching.py, test_retry_walltime.py, test_structured_outputs.py, test_evidence_loop.py, test_snapshot_scrub.py\n\n---\n\n### 9. ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS (BUILT vs ASPIRATIONAL)\n\n| Component | Status | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Scout (fetch) | **BUILT** | All 7 kinds implemented (local_mount, repo, awesome_list, topic_crawl, RSS, arXiv, discovery_queue); async per-host throttle; per-sweep budget respected |\n| Runner (static analysis) | **BUILT** | UUID-delimited prompt injection defense (O-8); artifact bundle JSON; no Docker sandbox (P4 deferred) |\n| Critics (A, B, C) | **BUILT** | Multi-family (Anthropic, Gemini, DeepSeek/Groq/Ollama); structured output (Wave L3); degrade fallbacks; cost metering per role |\n| Reconciler | **BUILT** | Fuses 2-3 verdicts; monotonic-toward-stricter evidence loop adoption |\n| Embedder | **BUILT** | 2D taxonomy (domain × complexity); gemini-embedding-2; precomputed placement |\n| Librarian | **BUILT** | Upserts artifacts; writes library/*.md; tracks validations + transcripts + bundles; security gate enforcement |\n| Evidence Loop | **BUILT** (SHADOW default) | Iterative rigor with precomputed score function (zero cost default); live re-score opt-in per-candidate |\n| Taste (interest ranking) | **BUILT** (Wave 4) | LLM-as-a-judge interest score; persisted to artifacts table; consumed by briefing |\n| Advisor (synthesis) | **BUILT** (Wave-C) | Replaces literature_reviewer; produces briefing paragraph + decision trees |\n| Security gate (ARF) | **BUILT** | Multi-detector suite (AST/behavioral/regex/provenance/secret-scan); enforcement at publish + library copy |\n| Models sweep | **BUILT** | smoke_runner, card_parser, benchmarks ingest; separate pipeline with own budget |\n| Dashboard | **BUILT** | Flask read-only; health signals, catalog browser, cost rollups, sweep drill-down; port 5001 |\n| Publisher | **BUILT** | Snapshot creation, changelog gen, git commit + push; PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER for benchmarks |\n| Cost tracking | **BUILT** | Per-call metering (costs table); per-role cells; monthly caps; Wave L1 cache sub-rates; Wave L6 batch discount |\n| Helping Hand MCP | **BUILT** | Session tracking, outcome telemetry, MoE judge integration (Wave A2) |\n| Prompt caching (L2) | **BUILT** | Gated by per-model minimum; system prefix + cache rates metered correctly |\n| Structured outputs (L3) | **BUILT** | Forced strict tool use + degrade path (plain text fallback) |\n| Adaptive thinking (L4) | **BUILT** | effort={low|medium|high|...}; thinking token folding; no budget_tokens (deprecated) |\n| Batch API (L6) | **BUILT** | critic_a batch sweep (50% discount); per-item failure degrade; optional (AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1) |\n| —— | | |\n| Docker sandbox (runner P4) | **DEFERRED** | P4+; runner is static analysis only |\n| Additional scout kinds (hub/marketplace/blog/forum/reddit) | **DEFERRED** | P4+ (currently 7/11 implemented) |\n| Prompt evolution / A/B testing | **NOT PLANNED** | Deep-think prompt isolation prevents regression; no active A/B harness |\n\n---\n\n### 10. RUNTIME EXAMPLE: Skills Sweep\n\n```bash\n# Cron-driven, 3x daily\npython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills  # live\npython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --dry-run  # testing\n\n# ~$0.56/sweep breakdown (approx):\n# - scout ~$0.03 (seed map fetch + URL fetch)\n# - runner ~$0.20 (top 2-8 items; Sonnet analysis)\n# - critic_a ~$0.08 (Sonnet review)\n# - critic_b ~$0.06 (Gemini review)\n# - critic_c ~$0.03 (DeepSeek/Groq, if key present)\n# - reconciler ~$0.06 (Sonnet fusion)\n# - librarian ~$0.02 (embedder + card write)\n# - sanitizer ~$0.008 (Haiku injections pass)\n# → Total: ~$0.48-0.56, well below $0.56 ceiling\n\n# Artifacts written: 15-25 per sweep (top-K swarm ~5-8 pass, static ~10-20)\n# Database rows: +N to artifacts, +N validations, +N costs, +N sources\n# Library tree: library/skills/{slug}/ markdown files + bundles/\n\n# Telemetry: logs/orchestrator-20260623T123456Z-skills.log\n```\n\n---\n\n### 11. CRITICAL INVARIANTS & GUARDS\n\n1. **No budget_tokens in Anthropic requests** — Wave L4 guard (_assert_no_budget_tokens) fails loudly on deprecated field; Opus 4.8 returns 400 if present\n2. **Thinking tokens always metered** — _fold_thinking_into_output() catches any separately-reported thinking and adds to output for cost; prevents repeat of May $118 incident\n3. **Structured outputs degrade gracefully** — on schema rejection, plain-text fallback (legacy parse path) prevents sweep abort\n4. **Per-role budget cells** — guardrail prevents any single role from dominating monthly spend; exceeding triggers partial status\n5. **Security gate enforcement** — single-owner gate.enforcement_clause() in roles/security/gate.py; applied at publish + library copy; fail-CLOSED (unscanned = non-servable)\n6. **Cache gating** — cache_control marker only attached when system prefix ≥ model's minimum (silent no-op below threshold)\n7. **Degrade counter** — per-run _DEGRADE_COUNT tracks Sonnet→Haiku fallbacks; orchestrator.close_run() → status='partial' if any\n8. **Critic C abstain tracking** — distinct from errors; morning briefing rolls up \"N fired / N abstained_no_key / N rate_limited\"\n9. **Dry-run byte-for-byte transparency** — walk pipeline structure identical, zero LLM calls, zero writes (test harness invariant)\n10. **Read-only dashboard** — opens kb/aurora.db READ-ONLY, never writes; safe to mount into Anchor\n\n---\n\n### 12. KEY FILES & ENTRY POINTS\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| orchestrator.py:main() | Nightly entry point; --sweep router; pipeline orchestrator |\n| llm.py:CostRecorder.record() | Single cost metering funnel |\n| llm.py:call_anthropic() | Anthropic message dispatch (retry + fallback + cache + structure + effort) |\n| llm.py:call_gemini() | Gemini dispatch (thinking off by default) |\n| publisher.py:main() | Snapshot + push after sweep |\n| aurora_dashboard.py:main() | Dashboard launcher (Flask server, port 5001) |\n| roles/scout.py:fan_out() | Seed map fetch coordinator |\n| roles/runner.py:run() | Static artifact analysis |\n| roles/critic_a.py:critique() | Security + correctness review |\n| roles/critic_b.py:critique() | Quality + clarity review |\n| roles/critic_c.py:critique() | Third-family consensus judge |\n| roles/reconciler.py:reconcile() | Critic fusion |\n| roles/librarian.py:upsert_artifact() | DB write gate (security enforcement) |\n| roles/evidence.py:run_evidence_loop() | Iterative rigor loop |\n| roles/security/gate.py:enforcement_clause() | Single-owner security gate SQL |\n| kb/schema.sql | Knowledge base schema (v3) |\n| kb/pricing.yaml | Cost pricing (vendors + rates + batch discount) |\n| dashboard/data/health.py:run_status() | Health signal aggregator |\n| exec_summary.py | Monthly cost rollup |\n| morning_briefing.py | Daily briefing render (16K LOC) |\n\n---\n\n### FINAL ASSESSMENT\n\n**Aurora is 100% built and production-ready.** All major sweeps (skills, tools, agents, models) have concrete implementations with:\n- End-to-end tested pipelines (96 test files)\n- Multi-layer cost controls (per-sweep, per-role, per-call)\n- Security hardening (injection defense, ARF scanning, gate enforcement)\n- Comprehensive telemetry (cost tracking, degrade visibility, health signals)\n- Safe degradation (fallbacks on every critical path)\n- Read-only observability (dashboard, exec summary, morning briefing)\n\nNo aspirational gaps in the core pipeline. Wave-A/B/C/L refinements are evolutionary hardening, not structural deferred features. The system runs 3x daily on cron with a $50/month spend cap and production monitoring — this is not a prototype."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f986a64-6630-4578-8cdf-92983029246b","uuid":"bc9e45f2-7efe-409c-ab8a-6e34a2d07727","timestamp":"2026-06-23T19:15:05.724Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Aurora project at C:\\dev\\aurora and report a structured map of its CODE architecture. I need to understand what is actually built vs aspirational.\n\nFocus on:\n1. orchestrator.py — the sweep entry point. What does --sweep {skills,tools,agents} do? What is the actual pipeline (discover → validate → catalog)? How many LLM calls per sweep roughly?\n2. llm.py — how all LLM calls funnel through. Does it have caching, batching, structured outputs? What model is the default? Retry logic? Cost tracking?\n3. publisher.py — what it builds and pushes.\n4. dashboard/ — the Flask read-only dashboard (port 5001). What does it show? What data sources does it read?\n5. The KB: kb/aurora.db schema — what tables exist, what's stored.\n6. Overall: how many Python modules, rough LOC, test coverage (any tests?), what's the dependency surface.\n\nReport concrete findings with file:line references. Quote key code where it reveals design decisions (e.g. the default model, caching presence/absence, error handling). Be precise about what EXISTS vs what is stubbed/TODO. Do not propose changes — just map reality. Medium-thorough exploration.","agentId":"aa527f3103a7c48dc","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create the final report:\n\n## Aurora Project: Code Architecture Map\n\n**Summary**: Aurora is a mature, production-quality nightly multi-agent sweep system (3 runs/day @ ~$0.56/sweep budget) that discovers, validates, and catalogs 350+ Claude skills, templates, tools, and open-source agents. The system is **fully built** with concrete implementations, not aspirational — deployment-ready with cost controls, security gates, and comprehensive testing.\n\n---\n\n### 1. ORCHESTRATOR PIPELINE\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/orchestrator.py` (1,456 lines)  \n**Entry Point**: `python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep {skills|tools|agents|models}`\n\n#### Sweep Modes\n- `--sweep skills` — Primary sweep covering Claude skills (typical nightly)\n- `--sweep tools` — MCP tools and other integrations\n- `--sweep agents` — Agent frameworks and autonomous systems\n- `--sweep models` — LLM model cards + benchmarks (separate pipeline)\n\n#### Execution Pipeline: Discover → Validate → Catalog\n\n**Main Walk (skills/tools/agents)** — orchestrator.walk_pipeline() [line 614]:\n\n1. **[1/8] Scout** (fetch phase)\n   - reads seed_map/{skills|tools|agents}.yaml (curated source URLs)\n   - Supports: local_mount, GitHub repos, RSS feeds, arXiv, awesome-lists, topic crawls\n   - Async per-host 1 req/sec throttle; respects AURORA_MAX_FETCH\n   - Yields ~50-200 FetchedSource objects per sweep\n\n2. **[2/8] Quarantine** (sanitization boundary)\n   - Wraps HTML/untrusted content with `<untrusted source=...>` markers\n   - Strips zero-width characters (injection defense)\n\n3. **[3.5/8] Sanitizer** (injection scrubbing)\n   - PromptArmor-style cheap-Haiku pass: detects prompt-injection patterns\n   - Fail-OPEN: outage never blocks sweep\n   - Records per-run injection count for telemetry\n\n4. **[4/8] Static Screener** (metadata-only qualification)\n   - Rejects: duplicates, broken links, pointer-only README links\n   - Returns ScannedCandidate with static_score (0..1)\n\n5. **[5/8] Split** (swarm vs. static-only routing)\n   - Top-K (default 2, env: AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K) → swarm (runner + 3 critics)\n   - Rest → static-only (embedder + librarian, no swarm)\n\n6. **[6/8] Swarm Path** (execution + multi-critic consensus) — for top-K only\n   - **Runner**: LLM-powered static analysis → {triggers, inputs, outputs, tool_surface, red_flags} artifact bundle (UUID-delimited to prevent injection)\n   - **Critic A** (Anthropic Sonnet 4.6, default): security + correctness skeptic on artifacts\n   - **Critic B** (Gemini 3.5-flash, default): quality + clarity evaluator\n   - **Critic C** (third-family judge: DeepSeek/Groq/Ollama, opt-in): cross-family consensus\n   - **Reconciler** (Anthropic Sonnet 4.6): fuses 2-3 verdicts → single pass/flag/reject\n   - **Evidence Loop** (Wave 3, SHADOW-default): iterative rigor via precomputed score function (zero LLM cost unless AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=1)\n   - Per-candidate budget check after each role; abort if PER_SWEEP_BUDGET exceeded\n\n7. **[7/8] Static Path** (embed + file, skip swarm)\n   - Embedder (Gemini 3.5-flash): places in 2D taxonomy (domain × complexity)\n   - Librarian: upserts artifact row, writes library/*.md\n\n8. **[8/8] Synthesis**\n   - Advisor (Wave-C): literature review → daily_syntheses + citation-grounded decision trees\n\n#### Budget Architecture\n\n**Per-sweep cap** [orchestrator.py:62]: $0.56 USD (50/30/3 = $50 monthly / 30 days / 3 sweeps)\n\n**Per-role budget cells** [lines 66-95] — sum < sweep_cap:\n- scout: 5%, sanitizer: 10%, runner: 35%, critic_a: 15%, critic_b: 15%, critic_c: 5%, reconciler: 10%, evidence_shadow: 10%, ranker_shadow: 8%, etc.\n- Pre-candidate + post-candidate checks via `_sweep_cost_so_far()`; exceeding any cell triggers `status='partial'`\n\n#### Shadow Features\n\n- **--retarget-shadow** (Wave 2): run high-signal sources + frontier ranker SHADOW-ONLY (never touch live KB)\n- **--dry-run**: walk pipeline with zero LLM calls, no network fetches\n- **--no-swarm**: skip runner+critics, embed/file all candidates (P2 mode)\n\n#### Models Sweep Pipeline\n\nSeparate walk_models_pipeline() [line ~1100]: smoke_runner (1-token live call per provider) → model_card_parser → screener → librarian → benchmarks ingest\n\n---\n\n### 2. LLM WRAPPER: llm.py\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/llm.py` (1,625 lines)\n\n#### Central LLM Call Funnels\n\n**call_anthropic()** [line 546]\n- Model default: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (if unspecified; most roles override via env)\n- Retry: G1 bucket — tenacity full-jitter exponential 1..60s, 5 attempts, wall-clock 60s max\n- Transient error classifiers: timeouts, connection drops, 429/5xx/529 (NOT 4xx like 400/401/403)\n- **Sonnet → Haiku fallback**: on retryable Sonnet exhaustion, degrade once to Haiku (180s total wall-clock via HAIKU_FALLBACK_DEADLINE_S)\n- **Degrade counter**: per-run _DEGRADE_COUNT bumped on fallback; orchestrator checks post-walk (degrades → status='partial')\n\n**Wave L1 (Prompt Caching)** [line 151-396]\n- Gated by MODEL_CACHE_MIN_TOKENS per model (Sonnet 4.6 = 2048 tokens)\n- cache_prefix_clears_minimum() prevents silent no-ops below threshold\n- cache_read_tokens priced ~0.1x input, cache_write_tokens ~1.25x input\n- CostRecorder.record() accepts cache_read_tokens / cache_write_tokens separately\n\n**Wave L2 (System Prefix Caching)** [line 677]\n- When cache_system=True + system prefix ≥ min threshold, wraps in structured block with ephemeral cache_control\n- Fallback (Sonnet→Haiku) reuses same `kw`, so degraded Haiku still benefits\n\n**Wave L3 (Structured Outputs)** [line 638-651]\n- Forced strict tool use: one tool (_STRUCTURED_TOOL_NAME = \"emit_result\") whose input_schema IS the caller's output_schema\n- model.messages.create() with tool_choice + strict:true → schema-guaranteed JSON\n- Degrade path: on schema rejection after Sonnet→Haiku exhaustion, retry ONCE as plain text (legacy parse path)\n- Cost: metered ONCE off whichever call succeeded\n\n**Wave L4 (Adaptive Thinking)** [line 652-662]\n- When effort={low|medium|high|xhigh|max}, request carries thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"} + output_config={\"effort\": effort}\n- NEVER budget_tokens (deprecated on 4.6+, removed on Opus 4.7/4.8 → 400)\n- _assert_no_budget_tokens() guard at dispatch funnel\n- Thinking tokens folded into metered output via _fold_thinking_into_output()\n\n**call_gemini()** [line 1053]\n- Model default: gemini-3.5-flash\n- Falls back to Anthropic Haiku if GEMINI_API_KEY unset, AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI=1, or AURORA_CRITIC_B_PROVIDER=local\n- thinking_config={\"thinking_budget\": 0} to disable hidden thinking (cost-audit fix for May $118 incident)\n- Fold thoughts_token_count into metered tokens_out (Google bills at output rate)\n\n**call_gemini_embedding()** [line 1136]\n- Model: models/gemini-embedding-2 (Wave I1 migration from Voyage, 10x cheaper)\n- Returns [] gracefully on missing API key or disabled flag\n\n**call_model()** [line 1179]\n- Unified dispatcher: routes to call_anthropic or call_gemini based on model ID\n- Wave L2/L3/L4: cache_system/output_schema/effort only honored on Anthropic path\n- Gemini path ignores schema (keeps free-form text response)\n\n#### Cost Recording: CostRecorder [line 257]\n\n```python\nclass CostRecorder:\n    def record(self, vendor, model, tokens_in, tokens_out,\n               cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0,\n               batch_mode=False) -> float:  # returns USD estimate\n```\n\n- Writes one row to `costs` table per call\n- Pricing loaded from kb/pricing.yaml (lookup_rates function)\n- Wave L1: cache tokens priced at sub-rates (cache_read ~0.1x, cache_write ~1.25x)\n- Wave L6: batch_mode=True applies 0.5x discount (Message Batches API)\n- Legacy 4-arg path (vendor, model, tin, tout) is byte-for-byte pre-Wave-L1\n\n#### Pricing Substrate\n\n**kb/pricing.yaml** structure:\n```yaml\nbatch_discount: 0.5\nvendors:\n  anthropic:\n    claude-sonnet-4-6:\n      tokens_in_per_million_usd: 3.0\n      tokens_out_per_million_usd: 15.0\n      cache_read_per_million_usd: 0.3\n      cache_write_per_million_usd: 3.75\n    # ...Haiku 4.5, Opus 4.6/4.8, with tokenizer_factor: 1.35 for 4.8\n  gemini:\n    gemini-3.5-flash: [rates + verified:false flag]\n    gemini-embedding-2: [rates + verified:false flag]\n    # ...Gemini 2.5-pro/flash, text-embedding-004\n  deepseek:\n    deepseek-chat: [0.27 in / 1.10 out]\n  groq:\n    llama-3.3-70b-versatile: [0.59 in / 0.79 out]\n  local:\n    default: [0.0 / 0.0]\n```\n\n**lookup_rates()** [line 108]: returns (in_per_million, out_per_million) with warn-once on missing  \n**tokenizer_factor()** [line 183]: 1.35 for Opus 4.8 (pre-call estimates only, never metered)  \n**batch_discount()** [line 247]: 0.5 top-level multiplier\n\n#### Batch API (Wave L6)\n\n**submit_anthropic_batch()** [line ~900]\n- Collects {slug → critic_a_prompt} into ONE Batches API submission\n- Polls with exponential backoff until all items succeed/failed/canceled\n- Per-item failure degrades to synchronous (stored in _ca_batch_texts dict, empty for failures)\n- Cost metered at 0.5x via batch_mode=True\n\n---\n\n### 3. PUBLISHER: publisher.py\n\n**File**: `/c/dev/aurora/publisher.py` (857 lines)\n\n**Lifecycle**: runs nightly after agents sweep (01:45 UTC daily per plan §16.2)\n\n#### Build → Push Workflow\n\n1. **Snapshot creation** (kb-snapshot.sqlite)\n   - Copies aurora.db → staging kb-snapshot.sqlite\n   - Scrubs transcripts, artifact bundles (private sweep data)\n   - Applies security gate: only CLEAN artifacts (security_status='CLEAN') persisted\n   - Deletes benchmark rows with null/non-allowed licenses or restricted sources (AA/OpenRouter)\n   - Runs VACUUM to compact\n\n2. **CHANGELOG generation**\n   - Derives daily entry from today's successful run (run.status != 'failed')\n   - Rolls up metrics: {fetched, screened, placed, flagged, usd_estimate}\n\n3. **Staging tree** (PUBLISH_ROOT = _publish/)\n   - Explicit allowlist: seed_maps, reports/, certain library/ dirs\n   - Filters library/{kind}/{slug}/ via _artifact_is_servable_in_snapshot() predicate\n   - Copies only CLEAN + non-retired artifacts\n\n4. **Git commit + push** (if not --dry-run)\n   - Requires GITHUB_PAT + GITHUB_REPO in .env\n   - Tags with YYYYMMDD, pushes to aurora-library repo\n   - Stores PAT lifecycle + last push metadata in publisher_state table\n\n#### Disposition Matrix\n\n- **Artifacts table** → SHIP (applies security gate enforcement §4.2)\n- **model_benchmarks** → PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER (scrub non-allowed)\n- **Transcripts, artifact bundles** → SCRUB (never ship)\n- **ranking_diffs** → SCRUB (internal diagnostics)\n- **hh_events / hh_sessions** → SHIP (user-facing telemetry)\n\n---\n\n### 4. KNOWLEDGE BASE: kb/aurora.db\n\n**Schema**: v3 (kb/schema.sql, 29,368 bytes)\n\n#### Core Tables (9 + satellites)\n\n1. **artifacts** (primary, ~356 rows)\n   - Fields: sweep, kind, slug, name, short_description, canonical_url, github_full_name, license, language\n   - Security (Wave C): security_status, security_scanned_arf_version, payload_sha256\n   - Embeddings (I1): description_vec (gemini-embedding-2 LE float32)\n   - Taste (Wave 4): interest_score, interest_why, interest_scored_at\n   - Frontier (W2): frontier_score (Wave 2, SHADOW-only)\n   - First_seen_at, last_verified_at, last_surfaced_in_summary_at, retired_at\n   - Index: kind, canonical_url, security_status\n   - UNIQUE(sweep, slug)\n\n2. **aliases** (URL deduplication)\n   - artifact_id, observed_url (UNIQUE), first_observed_at\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n3. **sources** (provenance per-doc)\n   - artifact_id, url, curator, kind, fetched_at, content_sha256\n   - Wave B3: excerpt, title, extraction_offsets (JSON {field: [start, end]})\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n4. **runs** (nightly sweeps)\n   - sweep (skills|tools|agents|models), started_at, finished_at, status\n   - budget_tokens_in, budget_tokens_out\n   - seed_map_snapshot (BLOB), prompt_template_shas (JSON), model_ids (JSON)\n   - critic_c_status, critic_c_calls, critic_c_errors\n   - Wave 1: sanitizer_n_injections\n   - Index: (sweep, started_at)\n\n5. **validations** (per-candidate eval)\n   - artifact_id, run_id, stage (screener|runner|critic_a|critic_b|critic_c|reconciler), verdict, score, rationale\n   - transcript_path, artifact_bundle_path\n   - Index: artifact_id, run_id\n\n6. **costs** (per-call metering)\n   - run_id, role, vendor, model_id, tokens_in, tokens_out, usd_estimate, recorded_at\n   - Wave L1: cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens (NULL on legacy 4-arg calls)\n   - batch_mode (1 = Message Batch)\n   - Index: run_id, (vendor, recorded_at)\n   - **Powers**: exec_summary.py MTD rollups, morning_briefing cost tables\n\n7. **embeddings** (2D taxonomy placement)\n   - artifact_id, domain_path, domain_depth, complexity_rank (0..4), embedded_at\n   - Index: artifact_id\n\n8. **neural_plasticity** (agents learning mechanics)\n   - artifact_id (PK), what_learns, learning_signal, what_is_modified, loss_or_objective, memory_model, etc.\n   - last_updated_at\n\n9. **hh_sessions / hh_events** (Helping Hand telemetry, Wave 3.2)\n   - hh_sessions: session_id, started_at, last_seen_at, scorer, match_calls\n   - hh_events: session_id, query_sha256, slug, artifact_kind, score, outcome, recorded_at\n   - Index: recorded_at, slug, session_id\n\n10. **models / model_benchmarks / model_smoke_tests** (Models sweep, v3.3)\n    - models: artifact_id, provider, family, version, context_in_tokens, max_output_tokens, pricing, etc.\n    - model_benchmarks: artifact_id, benchmark, score, source, license (CC3: PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER)\n    - model_smoke_tests: artifact_id, run_id, latency_ms, tokens, usd_estimate, error_msg\n\n11. **tool_install** (Wave A3 satellite)\n    - artifact_id (PK), install_method (npm|pip|cargo|...), invocation_kind (mcp-stdio|cli|...), mcp_config_json, etc.\n\n12. **Miscellaneous**: publisher_state, hh_interaction_buffer, hh_skill_upgrades, ranking_diffs (shadow)\n\n**Migrations**: kb/migrations/ directory (idempotent .sql files 0001-0027), applied at startup via kb.migrate\n\n---\n\n### 5. DASHBOARD: dashboard/ (Flask read-only)\n\n**Launch**: `python aurora_dashboard.py` → http://127.0.0.1:5001\n\n**Architecture**: Two-layer separation\n- `dashboard.data`: Flask-agnostic data layer (kb read-only, reports file reader) — imports ZERO aurora sweep code\n- `dashboard.web`: Flask blueprint factory over data layer → mountable on Anchor\n\n#### Data Layer (dashboard/data/, ~1,323 LOC)\n\n**Modules**:\n- **catalog.py**: artifact search, filter, detail (tags, aliases, sources, validations)\n- **costs.py**: cost rollups per-role, per-vendor, MTD tracking\n- **health.py**: run_status, noise_summary, degradation counts, rejects, log tails\n- **freshness.py**: fingerprint for change detection (poll optimization)\n- **models.py**: model cards, benchmark table, smoke test results\n- **reports.py**: file-based reports (decisions, state-reports, diffs)\n- **db.py**: read-only sqlite connection factory\n\n#### API Routes (blueprint.py, 13,774 bytes)\n\n- `/api/health` — liveness + full health object (runs, degradation, noise, backfills, logs)\n- `/api/health/summary` — human-readable alerts + signals (W4, never 500s)\n- `/api/health/detail?kind={noise|log|rejects|backfill}` — drill-down per signal\n- `/api/fingerprint` — hash for change detection\n- `/api/state` — machine state (seed maps, artifact counts by kind)\n- `/api/sweeps` — recent run list (W4)\n- `/api/sweep/{kind}/{date}` — detail for one sweep\n- `/api/morning` — morning briefing section (W2)\n- `/api/catalog/...` — artifact search, catalog stats (W5)\n- `/dashboard-static/*` — HTML/CSS/JS serving\n\n#### Static Assets (dashboard/web/static/)\n- dashboard.html — SPA entry point\n- Modern JS framework (observes /api/fingerprint for live polling)\n\n---\n\n### 6. DEPENDENCY SURFACE\n\n**pyproject.toml** — 52 direct dependencies:\n\n**Core Agents & LLM**:\n- claude-agent-sdk ≥0.1.81\n- anthropic ≥0.40\n- google-generativeai ≥0.8\n- openai ≥1.40 (local OpenAI-compatible fallback)\n\n**Async & Network**:\n- httpx ≥0.27 (async HTTP)\n- feedparser ≥6.0 (RSS)\n- tenacity ≥8.2 (retry with full-jitter)\n\n**Data & Config**:\n- pyyaml ≥6.0\n- pydantic ≥2.5\n- sqlite-utils ≥3.36\n- python-dotenv ≥1.0\n\n**Numerical**:\n- numpy ≥1.26\n- scikit-learn ≥1.4 (taxonomy placement)\n\n**Publishing & Reports**:\n- PyGithub ≥2.3 (git push)\n- reportlab ≥4.0 (PDF render, unicode-safe)\n- python-docx ≥1.0 (DOCX export)\n- fpdf2 ≥2.7 (legacy fallback)\n\n**Security & Extraction**:\n- detect-secrets ≥1.5 (secret scanning fallback)\n- langextract ≥1.2.0 (Google LangExtract adapter, soft-import, optional)\n\n**Dev**:\n- pytest ≥8.0, pytest-asyncio ≥0.23, ruff ≥0.5, mypy ≥1.10\n\n---\n\n### 7. CODE METRICS\n\n| Dimension | Count |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Total Python modules (excl. .venv) | 224 |\n| Top-level modules (orchestrator, llm, publisher, briefing_delivery, morning_briefing, exec_summary) | 6 |\n| **orchestrator.py** | 1,456 LOC |\n| **llm.py** | 1,625 LOC |\n| **publisher.py** | 857 LOC |\n| **morning_briefing.py** | 2,443 LOC |\n| Roles (roles/*.py) | 58 files, 13,574 LOC |\n| Security roles (roles/security/*.py) | 11 files, 4,855 LOC |\n| Dashboard data (dashboard/data/*.py) | 7 files, 1,323 LOC |\n| Test suite (tests/test_*.py) | **96 test files** |\n| KB migrations (kb/migrations/*.sql) | ~27 idempotent versions |\n\n---\n\n### 8. TEST COVERAGE\n\n**96 test files** covering:\n- **orchestrator**: walk_pipeline, budget cells, degrade counter, evidence loop, swarm/static split\n- **llm.py**: retry logic, cache gating, structured outputs, effort levels, batch API, degrade fallbacks\n- **publisher**: snapshot scrubbing, license filter, security gate, git push\n- **dashboard**: health signals, catalog queries, cost rollups, freshness\n- **roles**: scout, runner, critics, reconciler, sanitizer, quarantine, librarian, embedder, taste, advisor, evidence\n- **security**: ARF detector suite (AST rules, behavioral, regex, provenance), gate enforcement, sandbox confirmer\n- **models**: smoke testing, benchmarks, card parsing\n- **Helping Hand**: auto-mode, interaction buffer, session telemetry\n\nExamples: test_critic_c_cost.py, test_cost_cache_batch.py, test_per_role_budget.py, test_prompt_caching.py, test_retry_walltime.py, test_structured_outputs.py, test_evidence_loop.py, test_snapshot_scrub.py\n\n---\n\n### 9. ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS (BUILT vs ASPIRATIONAL)\n\n| Component | Status | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Scout (fetch) | **BUILT** | All 7 kinds implemented (local_mount, repo, awesome_list, topic_crawl, RSS, arXiv, discovery_queue); async per-host throttle; per-sweep budget respected |\n| Runner (static analysis) | **BUILT** | UUID-delimited prompt injection defense (O-8); artifact bundle JSON; no Docker sandbox (P4 deferred) |\n| Critics (A, B, C) | **BUILT** | Multi-family (Anthropic, Gemini, DeepSeek/Groq/Ollama); structured output (Wave L3); degrade fallbacks; cost metering per role |\n| Reconciler | **BUILT** | Fuses 2-3 verdicts; monotonic-toward-stricter evidence loop adoption |\n| Embedder | **BUILT** | 2D taxonomy (domain × complexity); gemini-embedding-2; precomputed placement |\n| Librarian | **BUILT** | Upserts artifacts; writes library/*.md; tracks validations + transcripts + bundles; security gate enforcement |\n| Evidence Loop | **BUILT** (SHADOW default) | Iterative rigor with precomputed score function (zero cost default); live re-score opt-in per-candidate |\n| Taste (interest ranking) | **BUILT** (Wave 4) | LLM-as-a-judge interest score; persisted to artifacts table; consumed by briefing |\n| Advisor (synthesis) | **BUILT** (Wave-C) | Replaces literature_reviewer; produces briefing paragraph + decision trees |\n| Security gate (ARF) | **BUILT** | Multi-detector suite (AST/behavioral/regex/provenance/secret-scan); enforcement at publish + library copy |\n| Models sweep | **BUILT** | smoke_runner, card_parser, benchmarks ingest; separate pipeline with own budget |\n| Dashboard | **BUILT** | Flask read-only; health signals, catalog browser, cost rollups, sweep drill-down; port 5001 |\n| Publisher | **BUILT** | Snapshot creation, changelog gen, git commit + push; PUBLISH-WITH-LICENSE-FILTER for benchmarks |\n| Cost tracking | **BUILT** | Per-call metering (costs table); per-role cells; monthly caps; Wave L1 cache sub-rates; Wave L6 batch discount |\n| Helping Hand MCP | **BUILT** | Session tracking, outcome telemetry, MoE judge integration (Wave A2) |\n| Prompt caching (L2) | **BUILT** | Gated by per-model minimum; system prefix + cache rates metered correctly |\n| Structured outputs (L3) | **BUILT** | Forced strict tool use + degrade path (plain text fallback) |\n| Adaptive thinking (L4) | **BUILT** | effort={low|medium|high|...}; thinking token folding; no budget_tokens (deprecated) |\n| Batch API (L6) | **BUILT** | critic_a batch sweep (50% discount); per-item failure degrade; optional (AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1) |\n| —— | | |\n| Docker sandbox (runner P4) | **DEFERRED** | P4+; runner is static analysis only |\n| Additional scout kinds (hub/marketplace/blog/forum/reddit) | **DEFERRED** | P4+ (currently 7/11 implemented) |\n| Prompt evolution / A/B testing | **NOT PLANNED** | Deep-think prompt isolation prevents regression; no active A/B harness |\n\n---\n\n### 10. RUNTIME EXAMPLE: Skills Sweep\n\n```bash\n# Cron-driven, 3x daily\npython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills  # live\npython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --dry-run  # testing\n\n# ~$0.56/sweep breakdown (approx):\n# - scout ~$0.03 (seed map fetch + URL fetch)\n# - runner ~$0.20 (top 2-8 items; Sonnet analysis)\n# - critic_a ~$0.08 (Sonnet review)\n# - critic_b ~$0.06 (Gemini review)\n# - critic_c ~$0.03 (DeepSeek/Groq, if key present)\n# - reconciler ~$0.06 (Sonnet fusion)\n# - librarian ~$0.02 (embedder + card write)\n# - sanitizer ~$0.008 (Haiku injections pass)\n# → Total: ~$0.48-0.56, well below $0.56 ceiling\n\n# Artifacts written: 15-25 per sweep (top-K swarm ~5-8 pass, static ~10-20)\n# Database rows: +N to artifacts, +N validations, +N costs, +N sources\n# Library tree: library/skills/{slug}/ markdown files + bundles/\n\n# Telemetry: logs/orchestrator-20260623T123456Z-skills.log\n```\n\n---\n\n### 11. CRITICAL INVARIANTS & GUARDS\n\n1. **No budget_tokens in Anthropic requests** — Wave L4 guard (_assert_no_budget_tokens) fails loudly on deprecated field; Opus 4.8 returns 400 if present\n2. **Thinking tokens always metered** — _fold_thinking_into_output() catches any separately-reported thinking and adds to output for cost; prevents repeat of May $118 incident\n3. **Structured outputs degrade gracefully** — on schema rejection, plain-text fallback (legacy parse path) prevents sweep abort\n4. **Per-role budget cells** — guardrail prevents any single role from dominating monthly spend; exceeding triggers partial status\n5. **Security gate enforcement** — single-owner gate.enforcement_clause() in roles/security/gate.py; applied at publish + library copy; fail-CLOSED (unscanned = non-servable)\n6. **Cache gating** — cache_control marker only attached when system prefix ≥ model's minimum (silent no-op below threshold)\n7. **Degrade counter** — per-run _DEGRADE_COUNT tracks Sonnet→Haiku fallbacks; orchestrator.close_run() → status='partial' if any\n8. **Critic C abstain tracking** — distinct from errors; morning briefing rolls up \"N fired / N abstained_no_key / N rate_limited\"\n9. **Dry-run byte-for-byte transparency** — walk pipeline structure identical, zero LLM calls, zero writes (test harness invariant)\n10. **Read-only dashboard** — opens kb/aurora.db READ-ONLY, never writes; safe to mount into Anchor\n\n---\n\n### 12. KEY FILES & ENTRY POINTS\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| orchestrator.py:main() | Nightly entry point; --sweep router; pipeline orchestrator |\n| llm.py:CostRecorder.record() | Single cost metering funnel |\n| llm.py:call_anthropic() | Anthropic message dispatch (retry + fallback + cache + structure + effort) |\n| llm.py:call_gemini() | Gemini dispatch (thinking off by default) |\n| publisher.py:main() | Snapshot + push after sweep |\n| aurora_dashboard.py:main() | Dashboard launcher (Flask server, port 5001) |\n| roles/scout.py:fan_out() | Seed map fetch coordinator |\n| roles/runner.py:run() | Static artifact analysis |\n| roles/critic_a.py:critique() | Security + correctness review |\n| roles/critic_b.py:critique() | Quality + clarity review |\n| roles/critic_c.py:critique() | Third-family consensus judge |\n| roles/reconciler.py:reconcile() | Critic fusion |\n| roles/librarian.py:upsert_artifact() | DB write gate (security enforcement) |\n| roles/evidence.py:run_evidence_loop() | Iterative rigor loop |\n| roles/security/gate.py:enforcement_clause() | Single-owner security gate SQL |\n| kb/schema.sql | Knowledge base schema (v3) |\n| kb/pricing.yaml | Cost pricing (vendors + rates + batch discount) |\n| dashboard/data/health.py:run_status() | Health signal aggregator |\n| exec_summary.py | Monthly cost rollup |\n| morning_briefing.py | Daily briefing render (16K LOC) |\n\n---\n\n### FINAL ASSESSMENT\n\n**Aurora is 100% built and production-ready.** All major sweeps (skills, tools, agents, models) have concrete implementations with:\n- End-to-end tested pipelines (96 test files)\n- Multi-layer cost controls (per-sweep, per-role, per-call)\n- Security hardening (injection defense, ARF scanning, gate enforcement)\n- Comprehensive telemetry (cost tracking, degrade visibility, health signals)\n- Safe degradation (fallbacks on every critical path)\n- Read-only observability (dashboard, exec summary, morning briefing)\n\nNo aspirational gaps in the core pipeline. Wave-A/B/C/L refinements are evolutionary hardening, not structural deferred features. The system runs 3x daily on cron with a $50/month spend cap and production monitoring — this is not a prototype."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":177643,"totalTokens":86386,"totalToolUseCount":45,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3062,"cache_read_input_tokens":75035,"output_tokens":8285,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_t